('e0b7271b-030c-5cf3-8cc3-512801cca668','35b148ad-045e-5f7b-bb2b-dfd896a5551e',5,'equipment','تجهیزات','technical','a piece of electronic equipment that can read information that is stored or recorded somewhere, for example on a card',null,null,'قطعه ای از تجهیزات الکترونیکی که می تواند اطلاعاتی را که در جایی ذخیره یا ثبت شده است، مثلاً روی کارت، بخواند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a slow/fast reader Her son was quite a slow reader.','a good reader He''s not a good reader but he wants to try a new story.','a poor reader (= someone who is not good at reading ) All these students had been judged to be poor readers.','a great reader (= someone who reads a lot of books ) My father was a great reader.','an avid/voracious reader (= someone who eagerly reads a lot of books ) She was an avid reader of historical novels.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('dd48e8fb-bfbf-58df-938f-d46e87545d5a','a6936718-380e-5213-8df5-91708cc7938f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an important teacher in a British university',null,null,'یک معلم مهم در یک دانشگاه بریتانیا','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a Reader in Sociology at Bristol University","translation":"یک خواننده در جامعه شناسی در دانشگاه بریستول","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000483023.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ef098cb7-3243-5bf9-8d61-2b503c8e89cc','7938b203-8b06-5c68-a2e8-f79f2566b546',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a weekly US newspaper printed in Chicago. It mainly covers news , entertainment , politics , and culture .',null,null,'یک روزنامه هفتگی ایالات متحده که در شیکاگو چاپ می شود. این عمدتا اخبار، سرگرمی، سیاست و فرهنگ را پوشش می دهد.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e89331e4-ebb0-5bc6-9fba-a428d31ddd0d','220d6202-af39-5b90-bb76-67b86539473c',1,'very','بسیار','spoken & written','very',null,null,'واقعاً، حقاً؛ خیلی (تأکید)؛ راستی؟',array['extremely']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a really good film","translation":"یک فیلم واقعا خوب","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604559.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was really cold last night.","translation":"دیشب واقعا سرد بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604560.mp3"},{"sentence":"He walks really slowly.","translation":"واقعا آهسته راه می رود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604561.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’m really, really sorry.","translation":"من واقعاً متاسفم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001770468.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('5e793006-9579-5872-90bc-53256a5b8c78','220d6202-af39-5b90-bb76-67b86539473c',2,'the real situation','وضعیت واقعی','spoken & written','used when you are talking about what actually happened or is true, rather than what people might wrongly think',null,null,'زمانی استفاده می‌شود که در مورد آنچه واقعاً اتفاق افتاده یا واقعی است صحبت می‌کنید، نه اینکه مردم ممکن است به اشتباه فکر کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Why don’t you tell us what really happened?","translation":"چرا به ما نمی گویید واقعا چه اتفاقی افتاده است؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000484899.mp3"},{"sentence":"Oliver’s not really her brother.","translation":"الیور واقعا برادرش نیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000484900.mp3"},{"sentence":"I never know what he’s really thinking.","translation":"من هرگز نمی دانم که او واقعاً به چه چیزی فکر می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604550.mp3"},{"sentence":"She seems unfriendly at first, but she’s really very nice.","translation":"او در ابتدا غیر دوستانه به نظر می رسد، اما او واقعاً بسیار خوب است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000484901.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('4998b40b-df3e-5603-af81-d391cba60965','220d6202-af39-5b90-bb76-67b86539473c',3,'definitely','قطعا','spoken & written','used to emphasize something you are saying',null,null,'برای تأکید بر چیزی که می گویید استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We really need that extra money.","translation":"ما واقعا به آن پول اضافی نیاز داریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604558.mp3"},{"sentence":"I really don’t mind.","translation":"واقعا برام مهم نیست","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000484908.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’m absolutely fine, Dad – really.","translation":"من کاملاً خوبم، بابا - واقعاً.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000484909.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('fde26bc6-8761-598a-8105-94283bf31806','220d6202-af39-5b90-bb76-67b86539473c',4,'not true','درست نیست','spoken & written','used in questions when you are asking someone if something is true and suggesting that you think it is not true',null,null,'هنگامی که از کسی می‌پرسید که آیا چیزی درست است یا خیر و نشان می‌دهد که فکر می‌کنید درست نیست، در سؤالات استفاده می‌شود',array['honestly']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Do you really think she’s doing this for your benefit?","translation":"آیا واقعا فکر می کنید که او این کار را به نفع شما انجام می دهد؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604555.mp3"},{"sentence":"Do you really expect me to believe that?","translation":"آیا واقعاً انتظار دارید که من این را باور کنم؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604556.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('0cefb7ca-3ca1-569a-8952-c9c7402ff332','220d6202-af39-5b90-bb76-67b86539473c',5,null,null,'spoken & written','used to show that you are surprised by what someone has said',null,null,'استفاده می شود تا نشان دهد که شما از آنچه کسی گفته است شگفت زده شده اید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘He’s Canadian.’ ‘Really?’","translation":"\"او کانادایی است.\" \"واقعا؟\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000484923.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘We had a great time in Florida.’ ‘Really? How lovely.’","translation":"«در فلوریدا لحظات خوبی داشتیم.» «واقعا؟ چقدر دوست داشتنی.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000484927.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘Glen can be such a jerk.’ ‘Yeah, really!’","translation":"«گلن می‌تواند چنین احمق باشد.» «آره، واقعاً!»","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000484932.mp3"},{"sentence":"Really, Larry, you might have told me!","translation":"واقعا لری شاید به من گفتی!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000484938.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('7a02a99f-a94a-5e63-8cc4-cd31cbef8492','220d6202-af39-5b90-bb76-67b86539473c',6,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'not really','واقعاً، حقاً؛ خیلی (تأکید)؛ راستی؟','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('17ff43a9-a861-5b13-8e0f-1f82c7e156cf','220d6202-af39-5b90-bb76-67b86539473c',7,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'should/ought really','واقعاً، حقاً؛ خیلی (تأکید)؛ راستی؟','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('fbbd137e-c260-5b4d-be21-fcac3775281a','220d6202-af39-5b90-bb76-67b86539473c',8,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'really and truly','واقعاً، حقاً؛ خیلی (تأکید)؛ راستی؟','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('d8007bde-16d3-5769-b956-b95a2061fca4','567010c0-7a63-5db1-a97f-8a7238c5db72',1,'cause','علت','formal','why something happens, or why someone does something','[ countable ]',null,'دلیل، سبب؛ دلیل (استدلال)؛ عقل (اندیشه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a reason We had many reasons to celebrate.','give a reason No reason was given for the change.','think of a reason/see a reason I see no reason why it shouldn’t work. I can’t think of any reason why she would want to leave.','explain the reasons for something Explain the reasons for your choice.','a good reason There is usually a good reason why the price is so cheap.','the main reason The main reason for the decline in the railways is lack of investment.','a major reason ( also a big reason informal ) His personality was a major reason for his success. A big reason for the decrease in smoking is the ban on cigarette advertising.','the real reason What do you think was the real reason for their decision?','a valid/legitimate reason (= a good and acceptable reason ) An employer can’t fire someone without a valid reason.','a compelling reason (= a very good reason for doing something ) There are compelling reasons to believe that this is true.','a simple reason (= one that is easy to understand ) I hate mobile phones, for the simple reason that it is now impossible to get away from them.','a logical reason People don’t always have logical reasons for the things they do.','the only reason The only reason he’s coming tonight is that I said you’d be here.','for legal/political/medical etc reasons The boy cannot be named for legal reasons.','for security reasons The road will be closed for security reasons.','for personal reasons He resigned for personal reasons.','for sentimental reasons (= because you like someone or something very much ) I wanted to keep the picture for sentimental reasons.','for obvious reasons This arrangement must be kept secret, for obvious reasons.','for no apparent reason (= for no obvious reason ) He tried to kill me for no apparent reason.','for some reason (or other) ( also for some unknown reason ) (= for a reason that you do not know ) For some reason she felt like crying. For some unknown reason, the curtains were always drawn.','for reasons best known to somebody (= used when you do not understand someone’s behaviour ) For reasons best known to herself, she decided to sell the house.','have your reasons (= have a secret reason for doing something ) ‘Why did he marry her?’ ‘He must have had his reasons.’']::text[],'[{"sentence":"People give different reasons for wanting to change jobs.","translation":"افراد دلایل مختلفی برای تمایل به تغییر شغل ارائه می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604632.mp3"},{"sentence":"We’d like to know the reason why she didn’t accept the job.","translation":"ما می خواهیم بدانیم که چرا او این کار را نپذیرفته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000485400.mp3"},{"sentence":"The reason I called was to ask about the plans for Saturday.","translation":"دلیل تماسم این بود که در مورد برنامه های شنبه بپرسم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000485394.mp3"},{"sentence":"He explained the reasons behind the decision.","translation":"او دلایل این تصمیم را توضیح داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604653.mp3"},{"sentence":"The bridge is closed for reasons of safety.","translation":"پل به دلایل ایمنی بسته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001295.mp3"},{"sentence":"This work gives me a reason to live.","translation":"این کار به من دلیلی برای زندگی می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001296.mp3"},{"sentence":"There is no reason whatsoever to doubt her story.","translation":"هیچ دلیلی برای شک در داستان او وجود ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa020198.mp3"},{"sentence":"a person disqualified by reason of age","translation":"فردی که به دلیل سن رد صلاحیت شده است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001298.mp3"}]'::jsonb,8),
('05eb5ffa-e995-55cb-8992-87f136ed091b','567010c0-7a63-5db1-a97f-8a7238c5db72',2,'good or fair','خوب یا منصفانه','spoken & written','a fact that makes it right or fair for someone to do something','[ uncountable ]',null,'واقعیتی که انجام کاری را برای کسی درست یا منصفانه می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a reason We had many reasons to celebrate.','give a reason No reason was given for the change.','think of a reason/see a reason I see no reason why it shouldn’t work. I can’t think of any reason why she would want to leave.','explain the reasons for something Explain the reasons for your choice.','a good reason There is usually a good reason why the price is so cheap.','the main reason The main reason for the decline in the railways is lack of investment.','a major reason ( also a big reason informal ) His personality was a major reason for his success. A big reason for the decrease in smoking is the ban on cigarette advertising.','the real reason What do you think was the real reason for their decision?','a valid/legitimate reason (= a good and acceptable reason ) An employer can’t fire someone without a valid reason.','a compelling reason (= a very good reason for doing something ) There are compelling reasons to believe that this is true.','a simple reason (= one that is easy to understand ) I hate mobile phones, for the simple reason that it is now impossible to get away from them.','a logical reason People don’t always have logical reasons for the things they do.','the only reason The only reason he’s coming tonight is that I said you’d be here.','for legal/political/medical etc reasons The boy cannot be named for legal reasons.','for security reasons The road will be closed for security reasons.','for personal reasons He resigned for personal reasons.','for sentimental reasons (= because you like someone or something very much ) I wanted to keep the picture for sentimental reasons.','for obvious reasons This arrangement must be kept secret, for obvious reasons.','for no apparent reason (= for no obvious reason ) He tried to kill me for no apparent reason.','for some reason (or other) ( also for some unknown reason ) (= for a reason that you do not know ) For some reason she felt like crying. For some unknown reason, the curtains were always drawn.','for reasons best known to somebody (= used when you do not understand someone’s behaviour ) For reasons best known to herself, she decided to sell the house.','have your reasons (= have a secret reason for doing something ) ‘Why did he marry her?’ ‘He must have had his reasons.’']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There is no reason to panic.","translation":"دلیلی برای وحشت وجود ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000485446.mp3"},{"sentence":"She has reason to feel guilty.","translation":"او دلیلی برای احساس گناه دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604659.mp3"},{"sentence":"We have reason to believe that the goods were stolen.","translation":"ما دلایلی داریم که باور کنیم این کالا به سرقت رفته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001604665.mp3"},{"sentence":"I know I’m late, but that’s no reason to shout at me.","translation":"می دانم که دیر آمده ام، اما این دلیلی برای فریاد زدن سر من نیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000485453.mp3"},{"sentence":"Under the circumstances, we had every reason (= had very good reasons ) to be suspicious.","translation":"در این شرایط، ما هر دلیلی داشتیم (= دلایل بسیار خوبی داشتیم) برای مشکوک شدن.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000485450.mp3"},{"sentence":"Natalie was alarmed by the news, and with reason.","translation":"ناتالی از این خبر نگران شد و دلیلی هم داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000485457.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('cff3198d-f0c1-538e-bb3e-59bec6853d40','567010c0-7a63-5db1-a97f-8a7238c5db72',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'all the more reason why/to do something','دلیل، سبب؛ دلیل (استدلال)؛ عقل (اندیشه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a reason We had many reasons to celebrate.','give a reason No reason was given for the change.','think of a reason/see a reason I see no reason why it shouldn’t work. I can’t think of any reason why she would want to leave.','explain the reasons for something Explain the reasons for your choice.','a good reason There is usually a good reason why the price is so cheap.','the main reason The main reason for the decline in the railways is lack of investment.','a major reason ( also a big reason informal ) His personality was a major reason for his success. A big reason for the decrease in smoking is the ban on cigarette advertising.','the real reason What do you think was the real reason for their decision?','a valid/legitimate reason (= a good and acceptable reason ) An employer can’t fire someone without a valid reason.','a compelling reason (= a very good reason for doing something ) There are compelling reasons to believe that this is true.','a simple reason (= one that is easy to understand ) I hate mobile phones, for the simple reason that it is now impossible to get away from them.','a logical reason People don’t always have logical reasons for the things they do.','the only reason The only reason he’s coming tonight is that I said you’d be here.','for legal/political/medical etc reasons The boy cannot be named for legal reasons.','for security reasons The road will be closed for security reasons.','for personal reasons He resigned for personal reasons.','for sentimental reasons (= because you like someone or something very much ) I wanted to keep the picture for sentimental reasons.','for obvious reasons This arrangement must be kept secret, for obvious reasons.','for no apparent reason (= for no obvious reason ) He tried to kill me for no apparent reason.','for some reason (or other) ( also for some unknown reason ) (= for a reason that you do not know ) For some reason she felt like crying. For some unknown reason, the curtains were always drawn.','for reasons best known to somebody (= used when you do not understand someone’s behaviour ) For reasons best known to herself, she decided to sell the house.','have your reasons (= have a secret reason for doing something ) ‘Why did he marry her?’ ‘He must have had his reasons.’']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('864893a7-a01a-5224-a8bc-816a4a426257','567010c0-7a63-5db1-a97f-8a7238c5db72',4,'good judgment','قضاوت خوب','spoken & written','sensible judgment and understanding','[ uncountable ]',null,'قضاوت و درک معقول',array['sense']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a reason We had many reasons to celebrate.','give a reason No reason was given for the change.','think of a reason/see a reason I see no reason why it shouldn’t work. I can’t think of any reason why she would want to leave.','explain the reasons for something Explain the reasons for your choice.','a good reason There is usually a good reason why the price is so cheap.','the main reason The main reason for the decline in the railways is lack of investment.','a major reason ( also a big reason informal ) His personality was a major reason for his success. A big reason for the decrease in smoking is the ban on cigarette advertising.','the real reason What do you think was the real reason for their decision?','a valid/legitimate reason (= a good and acceptable reason ) An employer can’t fire someone without a valid reason.','a compelling reason (= a very good reason for doing something ) There are compelling reasons to believe that this is true.','a simple reason (= one that is easy to understand ) I hate mobile phones, for the simple reason that it is now impossible to get away from them.','a logical reason People don’t always have logical reasons for the things they do.','the only reason The only reason he’s coming tonight is that I said you’d be here.','for legal/political/medical etc reasons The boy cannot be named for legal reasons.','for security reasons The road will be closed for security reasons.','for personal reasons He resigned for personal reasons.','for sentimental reasons (= because you like someone or something very much ) I wanted to keep the picture for sentimental reasons.','for obvious reasons This arrangement must be kept secret, for obvious reasons.','for no apparent reason (= for no obvious reas