('7ab58c60-81ca-5ad2-8137-a9d97f28db6e','fa98909e-ddcf-54b8-83ac-2def50402672',11,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'set/put the record straight','سابقه، سابقه (کار)؛ رکورد (بازی)؛ پرونده (پلیس)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('5c8ae90c-36ac-5b29-866e-6f4558bc9e0e','fdf01b70-2c89-566f-b8ba-b3fd6186d5d8',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to write information down or store it in a computer or on film so that it can be looked at in the future','[ transitive ]',null,'ثبت کردن؛ ضبط کردن (صدا)؛ ثبت کردن (پرونده)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Her husband made her record every penny she spent.","translation":"شوهرش هر پنی را که خرج می کرد رکورد زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001771404.mp3"},{"sentence":"He recorded that the operation was successful.","translation":"او ثبت کرد که این عملیات موفقیت آمیز بوده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001876466.mp3"},{"sentence":"In 1892 it is recorded that the weather became so cold that the river froze over.","translation":"در سال 1892 گزارش شده است که هوا به قدری سرد شد که رودخانه یخ زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000761540.mp3"},{"sentence":"The coroner recorded a verdict of accidental death.","translation":"پزشکی قانونی حکم مرگ تصادفی را ثبت کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001592863.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('514d1755-30c1-51be-9423-eaea590f5911','fdf01b70-2c89-566f-b8ba-b3fd6186d5d8',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to store music, sound, television programmes etc on a disc or tape so that people can listen to them or watch them again','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'برای ذخیره موسیقی، صدا، برنامه های تلویزیونی و غیره بر روی یک دیسک یا نوار به طوری که مردم بتوانند به آنها گوش دهند یا دوباره آنها را تماشا کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The group has just recorded a new album.","translation":"این گروه به تازگی آلبوم جدیدی را ضبط کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000761553.mp3"},{"sentence":"Is the machine still recording?","translation":"آیا دستگاه هنوز ضبط می کند؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000761554.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’ll record the film and we can all watch it later.","translation":"من فیلم را ضبط می کنم و همه می توانیم بعداً آن را تماشا کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000761555.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('0cd13d9a-52ff-5ab4-a07f-522cff5947e5','fdf01b70-2c89-566f-b8ba-b3fd6186d5d8',3,null,null,'spoken & written','if an instrument records the size , speed, temperature etc of something, it measures it and keeps that information','[ transitive ]',null,'اگر ابزاری اندازه، سرعت، دما و غیره چیزی را ثبت کند، آن را اندازه گیری کرده و آن اطلاعات را نگه می دارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Wind speeds of up to 100 mph have been recorded.","translation":"سرعت باد تا 100 مایل در ساعت ثبت شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000761560.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('083a4116-1d7f-5f33-8be7-30572efa3d69','beb3faf3-6fda-5a70-8c76-f502e59c6d25',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make something smaller or less in size , amount , or price','[ transitive ]',null,'کاهش دادن، کم کردن (مقدار)؛ ساده کردن (به کسر)',array['cut']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['greatly/substantially/considerably reduce He has greatly reduced the political power of the armed forces.','significantly reduce Their symptoms were significantly reduced.','dramatically/drastically reduce They are committed to drastically reducing the size and cost of government.','sharply reduce Medical progress has sharply reduced death rates.','gradually reduce The aim is to gradually reduce the number of troops in the area.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The governor announced a new plan to reduce crime.","translation":"استاندار از طرح جدید کاهش جرایم خبر داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001540270.mp3"},{"sentence":"The helmet law should reduce injuries in motorcycle accidents.","translation":"قانون کلاه ایمنی باید صدمات ناشی از تصادفات موتورسیکلت را کاهش دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000763191.mp3"},{"sentence":"Small businesses will need to reduce costs in order to survive.","translation":"کسب و کارهای کوچک برای ادامه حیات باید هزینه ها را کاهش دهند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001540271.mp3"},{"sentence":"The workforce has been reduced by half.","translation":"نیروی کار به نصف کاهش یافته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000763194.mp3"},{"sentence":"All the shirts were reduced to £10.","translation":"تمام پیراهن ها به 10 پوند کاهش یافت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001540274.mp3"},{"sentence":"The new bridge should reduce travelling time from 50 minutes to 15 minutes.","translation":"پل جدید باید زمان سفر را از 50 دقیقه به 15 دقیقه کاهش دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001540275.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('f8d06dde-e823-52d2-8e71-17eff7e91f16','beb3faf3-6fda-5a70-8c76-f502e59c6d25',2,null,null,'spoken & written','if you reduce a liquid , or if it reduces, you boil it so that there is less of it','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'اگر مایعی را کم کنید، یا اگر کم شود، آن را بجوشانید تا کم شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['greatly/substantially/considerably reduce He has greatly reduced the political power of the armed forces.','significantly reduce Their symptoms were significantly reduced.','dramatically/drastically reduce They are committed to drastically reducing the size and cost of government.','sharply reduce Medical progress has sharply reduced death rates.','gradually reduce The aim is to gradually reduce the number of troops in the area.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('8a0a0519-d43b-5e3b-9636-e628225ca98c','beb3faf3-6fda-5a70-8c76-f502e59c6d25',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to become thinner by losing weight','[ intransitive ]',null,'برای لاغر شدن با کاهش وزن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['greatly/substantially/considerably reduce He has greatly reduced the political power of the armed forces.','significantly reduce Their symptoms were significantly reduced.','dramatically/drastically reduce They are committed to drastically reducing the size and cost of government.','sharply reduce Medical progress has sharply reduced death rates.','gradually reduce The aim is to gradually reduce the number of troops in the area.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('8f54aa1d-c188-58f7-8aff-3c21807f29d8','beb3faf3-6fda-5a70-8c76-f502e59c6d25',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be in reduced circumstances','کاهش دادن، کم کردن (مقدار)؛ ساده کردن (به کسر)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['greatly/substantially/considerably reduce He has greatly reduced the political power of the armed forces.','significantly reduce Their symptoms were significantly reduced.','dramatically/drastically reduce They are committed to drastically reducing the size and cost of government.','sharply reduce Medical progress has sharply reduced death rates.','gradually reduce The aim is to gradually reduce the number of troops in the area.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('6afb490f-7285-5587-9bf2-cbaa35fcb5b2','b65cd852-0fce-56d9-a066-7fc8a3adb4eb',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a change or changes made to a system or organization in order to improve it',null,null,'اصلاحات، اصلاح (سامانه)؛ اصلاح (تأسیس)؛ اصلاح (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['economic reform The prime minister has promised to push ahead with economic reform.','political/democratic/constitutional reform He stressed that democratic reform could not be achieved overnight.','tax reform The chancellor''s proposals for tax reform met strong resistance in the Commons.','education reform Teachers say the government''s education reforms are causing stress.','a major reform He called for a major reform of the drug laws.','radical reform (= very big and important changes ) His government adopted a policy of radical reform.','fundamental reform (= changes to the most basic and important parts of something ) He wants fundamental reform of the EU''s agricultural policy.','far-reaching/sweeping reforms (= reforms that affect many things or have a great effect ) The new government instituted a series of far-reaching reforms.','make/carry out reforms They haven''t made any real reforms.','introduce reforms They increased pressure on the government to introduce political reforms.','push through reforms (= make them happen ) He has so far failed to push through much-needed economic reforms.','implement reforms (= carry out planned reforms ) Much will depend on how local managers implement the reforms.','a package/programme of reforms A package of reforms was approved by the National Assembly on April 12.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a reform of the legal system","translation":"اصلاح نظام حقوقی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661649.mp3"},{"sentence":"The government announced a much-needed programme of economic reform.","translation":"دولت برنامه بسیار مورد نیاز اصلاحات اقتصادی را اعلام کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001772345.mp3"},{"sentence":"Reforms were made to revive the economy.","translation":"اصلاحات برای احیای اقتصاد انجام شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661655.mp3"},{"sentence":"The prime minister is calling for sweeping reforms of the NHS.","translation":"نخست وزیر خواستار اصلاحات گسترده در NHS است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661662.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('bcfa2e3f-6138-5bae-9d3c-84851b3981c1','1c038dbc-8f70-5225-aaf3-f772f96ddf0f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to improve a system, law , organization etc by making a lot of changes to it, so that it operates in a fairer or more effective way','[ transitive ]',null,'برای بهبود یک سیستم، قانون، سازمان و غیره با ایجاد تغییرات زیاد در آن، به طوری که به شیوه ای عادلانه تر یا موثرتر عمل کند.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"plans to radically reform the tax system","translation":"برنامه ریزی برای اصلاح اساسی سیستم مالیاتی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000768814.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('e691943f-4035-54a8-b862-78b641fce279','1c038dbc-8f70-5225-aaf3-f772f96ddf0f',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to change your behaviour and become a better person, or to make someone do this','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'برای تغییر رفتار و تبدیل شدن به فرد بهتر یا مجبور کردن کسی به این کار','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Greeley says he’s a genuinely reformed character .","translation":"گریلی می گوید که او یک شخصیت واقعاً اصلاح شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661644.mp3"},{"sentence":"a reformed criminal","translation":"یک جنایتکار اصلاح شده","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661648.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('356cb9b6-b8a2-56e4-a2f4-9bdea8adbc3d','fa9b66c9-591b-5cc2-b82c-84d1d808d4c3',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to say firmly that you will not do something that someone has asked you to do','[ intransitive ]',null,'سر باز زدن، امتناع کردن (از)؛ رد کردن (پیشنهاد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['stubbornly refuse He stubbornly refused to pay the fine.','adamantly refuse formal (= in a determined way ) They are still adamantly refusing to release the data to the general public.','steadfastly refuse (= refuse, and continue to refuse ) She steadfastly refused to marry him.','consistently refuse Politicians have consistently refused to listen to us.','flatly refuse (= in a firm and definite way ) He flatly refused to tell me anything.','simply refuse (= used for emphasis ) Some children simply refuse to do what they’re told.','refuse point-blank (= directly and without explanation ) I refused point-blank to let him in.','somebody can hardly refuse (= it would be unreasonable or very difficult to refuse ) Going out was the last thing I wanted to do, but I could hardly refuse.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She asked him to leave, but he refused.","translation":"از او خواست که برود، اما او نپذیرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000769291.mp3"},{"sentence":"The chairman refused to answer any more questions.","translation":"رئیس از پاسخ دادن به سوالات دیگر خودداری کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00721.mp3"},{"sentence":"I absolutely refuse to take part in anything illegal.","translation":"من مطلقاً از شرکت در هر کاری غیرقانونی امتناع می کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000769294.mp3"},{"sentence":"Mom flatly refused to go back into the hospital.","translation":"مامان قاطعانه از رفتن به بیمارستان امتناع کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000769298.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('ddaa9c79-8d80-5a3c-9bae-3815bd5d7f43','fa9b66c9-591b-5cc2-b82c-84d1d808d4c3',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to say no to something that you have been offered','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'نه گفتن به چیزی که به شما پیشنهاد شده است',array['turn down']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['stubbornly refuse He stubbornly refused to pay the fine.','adamantly refuse formal (= in a determined way ) They are still adamantly refusing to release the data to the general public.','steadfastly refuse (= refuse, and continue to refuse ) She steadfastly refused to marry him.','consistently refuse Politicians have consistently refused to listen to us.','flatly refuse (= in a firm and definite way ) He flatly refused to tell me anything.','simply refuse (= used for emphasis ) Some children simply refuse to do what they’re told.','refuse point-blank (= directly and without explanation ) I refused point-blank to let him in.','somebody can hardly refuse (= it would be unreasonable or very difficult to refuse ) Going out was the last thing I wanted to do, but I could hardly refuse.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She refused a second piece of cake.","translation":"او تکه دوم کیک را رد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000769308.mp3"},{"sentence":"The offer seemed too good to refuse .","translation":"این پیشنهاد برای رد کردن خیلی خوب به نظر می رسید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661733.mp3"},{"sentence":"When they offered all that money, I could hardly refuse , could I? (= it was very unlikely that you would refuse )","translation":"وقتی آنها این همه پول را پیشنهاد کردند، من به سختی می توانستم رد کنم، آیا می توانم؟ (= خیلی بعید بود که رد کنید)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00722.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('2d697378-57ab-5a54-a4d0-22ea5dea8ffd','fa9b66c9-591b-5cc2-b82c-84d1d808d4c3',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to not give or allow someone something that they want, especially when they have asked for it officially','[ transitive ]',null,'به کسی چیزی را که می‌خواهد نداده یا اجازه نمی‌دهد، مخصوصاً وقتی آن را رسماً درخواست کرده باشد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['stubbornly refuse He stubbornly refused to pay the fine.','adamantly refuse formal (= in a determined way ) They are still adamantly refusing to release the data to the general public.','steadfastly refuse (= refuse, and continue to refuse ) She steadfastly refused to marry him.','consistently refuse Politicians have consistently refused to listen to us.','flatly refuse (= in a firm and definite way ) He flatly refused to tell me anything.','simply refuse (= used for emphasis ) Some children simply refuse to do what they’re told.','refuse point-blank (= directly and without explanation ) I refused point-blank to let him in.','somebody can hardly refuse (= it would be unreasonable or very difficult to refuse ) Going out was the last thing I wanted to do, but I could hardly refuse.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She was refused a work permit.","translation":"اجازه کار به او رد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661737.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('71564c20-1ac9-5949-8610-dac83b1d3039','d3ec4558-9b15-5a8f-a575-4f26c94b5816',1,null,null,'spoken & written','waste material that has been thrown away',null,null,'مواد زائد دور ریخته شده','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a refuse dump","translation":"زباله دان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661744.mp3"},{"sentence":"refuse collection","translation":"جمع آوری زباله","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001876610.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('ed163294-d492-5062-bb49-7e2ad2c55764','16529df6-75b6-58fd-beb6-8296f7f34099',1,'admiration/respect','تحسین / احترام','spoken & written','respect and admiration for someone or something','[ uncountable ]',null,'احترام، اکرام؛ توجه (به)؛ احترام (تأکید)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['high regard The players have a very high regard for their manager.','low regard This might explain the low regard in which the president is held.','mutual regard (= which people feel for each other ) There seems to have been a genuine mutual regard between the two leaders.','considerable regard (= fairly high regard ) Eliot had considerable regard for Collingwood.','hold somebody/something in high regard Doctors are held in high regard by society.','have a high regard for somebody/something I had the highest regard for him.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Jan’s regard for his great talent","translation":"جان به استعداد بزرگش احترام می گذارد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000769509.mp3"},{"sentence":"Burt had high regard for his old law professor, Dr. Finch (= he respected him a lot ) .","translation":"برت به استاد حقوق قدیمی خود، دکتر فینچ احترام زیادی قائل بود (= او به او احترام زیادی می گذاشت).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661796.mp3"},{"sentence":"The voters hold her in high regard (= respect or admire her ) .","translation":"رای دهندگان به او احترام زیادی قائلند (= احترام می گذارند یا او را تحسین می کنند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661802.mp3"},{"sentence":"Teachers are held in low regard in this society (= are not respected or admired ) .","translation":"معلمان در این جامعه مورد احترام قرار نمی گیرند (= مورد احترام و تحسین نیستند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661809.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('cd002a28-26f6-5172-a509-4d9c68da4da9','16529df6-75b6-58fd-beb6-8296f7f34099',2,'attention/consideration','توجه / توجه','formal','attention or consideration that is shown towards someone or something','[ uncountable ]',null,'توجه یا توجهی که نسبت به کسی یا چیزی نشان داده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She has no regard for other people’s feelings.","translation":"او هیچ توجهی به احساسات دیگران ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000769522.mp3"},{"sentence":"One must show proper regard for the law.","translation":"باید به قانون توجه مناسب نشان داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661815.mp3"},{"sentence":"The present administration has demonstrated little regard for environmental issues.","translation":"دولت فعلی توجه کمی به مسائل زیست محیطی نشان داده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001316.mp3"},{"sentence":"All students must have access to quality education without regard to wealth or class.","translation":"همه دانش آموزان باید بدون توجه به ثروت یا طبقه به آموزش با کیفیت دسترسی داشته باشند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661822.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('2beccad7-01dc-573f-9534-831fd5821c5b','16529df6-75b6-58fd-beb6-8296f7f34099',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'with/in regard to something','احترام، اکرام؛ توجه (به)؛ احترام (تأکید)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('8607a53f-1c2d-5c54-a587-9f98e653b14c','16529df6-75b6-58fd-beb6-8296f7f34099',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'in this/that regard','احترام، اکرام؛ توجه (به)؛ احترام (تأکید)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('366892d0-d234-553b-a02d-5c364301bca9','16529df6-75b6-58fd-beb6-8296f7f34099',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'regards','احترام، اکرام؛ توجه (به)؛ احترام (تأکید)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('5c78720a-7494-5880-986b-7a3cf4c288b2','16529df6-75b6-58fd-beb6-8296f7f34099',6,null,null,'literary','a long look without moving your eyes','[ singular ]',null,'نگاهی طولانی بدون حرکت چشم','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e77b2ede-35f9-5d79-9443-844a4a844885','6ee2bb51-54be-5567-956a-70e9c5e10f29',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to think about someone or something in a particular way','[ not in progressive ]',null,'توجه داشتن (به)؛ پنداشتن (به‌طور)؛ ملاحظه کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Paul seemed to regard sex as sinful and immoral.","translation":"به نظر می رسید پولس رابطه جنسی را گناه آلود و غیراخلاقی می دانست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000769573.mp3"},{"sentence":"Edith was widely regarded as (= considered by many people to be ) eccentric.","translation":"ادیت به طور گسترده ای به عنوان (= توسط بسیاری از مردم به عنوان) عجیب و غریب در نظر گرفته شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661831.mp3"},{"sentence":"His work is highly regarded (= regarded as very good ) by art experts.","translation":"کار او بسیار مورد توجه (= بسیار خوب تلقی می شود) توسط کارشناسان هنری است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661836.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('b62e9764-6e1e-5c6d-8760-139b8f9e5251','6ee2bb51-54be-5567-956a-70e9c5e10f29',2,null,null,'formal','to look at someone or something in a particular way',null,null,'به کسی یا چیزی به شکلی خاص نگاه کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She stood back and regarded him coldly.","translation":"او عقب ایستاد و با خونسردی به او نگاه کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661841.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('296bd5cb-58b7-53c8-9fce-2e3f7fc40e04','6ee2bb51-54be-5567-956a-70e9c5e10f29',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'as regards something','توجه داشتن (به)؛ پنداشتن (به‌طور)؛ ملاحظه کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('fb998706-38ea-5e83-9929-582317d04b5e','c6d6901d-905c-54bd-a588-6ec6536d0f79',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a government, especially one that was not elected fairly or that you disapprove of for some other reason',null,null,'رژیم (حکومت)؛ رژیم (دیکتاتوری)؛ رژیم (محدود)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a political regime All political regimes attempt to manipulate the media.','a military regime The military regime arrested anyone who dared to speak against it.','a totalitarian regime (= in which people are totally controlled by a government that is not elected ) Totalitarian regimes ban books they disapprove of.','an authoritarian regime (= with very strong control ) The post-war authoritarian regimes of eastern Europe have been replaced by democratically elected governments.','a communist regime the collapse of communist regimes in eastern Europe','a fascist regime Mussolini ''s fascist regime in Italy','a democratic regime the establishment of a liberal democratic regime','an oppressive/repressive regime (= powerful, cruel, and unfair ) That country was held fast in the grip of an oppressive regime.','a brutal regime (= cruel and violent ) Many asylum seekers have fled from brutal regimes.','a corrupt regime (= dishonest ) Much of the aid that the Americans sent lined the pockets of his corrupt regime.','overthrow/topple a regime (= remove it from power ) In 1979, Tanzanian forces overthrew the regime of Ugandan dictator Idi Amin.','oppose a regime (= fight or compete against it ) People who opposed the regime were executed in a wave of political violence.','a regime comes to power He criticised European leaders for supporting a regime that came to power through violence.','a regime collapses/falls (= loses power ) Authoritarian regimes tend to collapse in times of economic hardship.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The regime got rid of most of its opponents.","translation":"رژیم از شر اکثر مخالفان خود خلاص شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000769734.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('0184d9c0-c883-5814-8b67-f7f83f7010e0','c6d6901d-905c-54bd-a588-6ec6536d0f79',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a particular system – used especially when talking about a previous system, or one that has just been introduced',null,null,'یک سیستم خاص - به ویژه هنگامی که در مورد یک سیستم قبلی صحبت می شود یا سیستمی که به تازگی معرفی شده است استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a political regime All political regimes attempt to manipulate the media.','a military regime The military regime arrested anyone who dared to speak against it.','a totalitarian regime (= in which people are totally controlled by a government that is not elected ) Totalitarian regimes ban books they disapprove of.','an authoritarian regime (= with very strong control ) The post-war authoritarian regimes of eastern Europe have been replaced by democratically elected governments.','a communist regime the collapse of communist regimes in eastern Europe','a fascist regime Mussolini ''s fascist regime in Italy','a democratic regime the establishment of a liberal democratic regime','an oppressive/repressive regime (= powerful, cruel, and unfair ) That country was held fast in the grip of an oppressive regime.','a brutal regime (= cruel and violent ) Many asylum seekers have fled from brutal regimes.','a corrupt regime (= dishonest ) Much of the aid that the Americans sent lined the pockets of his corrupt regime.','overthrow/topple a regime (= remove it from power ) In 1979, Tanzanian forces overthrew the regime of Ugandan dictator Idi Amin.','oppose a regime (= fight or compete against it ) People who opposed the regime were executed in a wave of political violence.','a regime comes to power He criticised European leaders for supporting a regime that came to power through violence.','a regime collapses/falls (= loses power ) Authoritarian regimes tend to collapse in times of economic hardship.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Under the new regime, all sheep and cattle will be regularly tested for disease.","translation":"تحت رژیم جدید، همه گوسفندان و گاوها به طور منظم از نظر بیماری آزمایش خواهند شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001319.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('53cc5a8f-e655-5c4a-aeb6-893e50742a02','c6d6901d-905c-54bd-a588-6ec6536d0f79',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a special plan of food, exercise etc that is intended to improve your health',null,null,'برنامه خاصی از غذا، ورزش و غیره که برای بهبود سلامت شما در نظر گرفته شده است',array['regimen']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a political regime All political regimes attempt to manipulate the media.','a military regime The military regime arrested anyone who dared to speak against it.','a totalitarian regime (= in which people are totally controlled by a government that is not elected ) Totalitarian regimes ban books they disapprove of.','an authoritarian regime (= with very strong control ) The post-war authoritarian regimes of eastern Europe have been replaced by democratically elected governments.','a communist regime the collapse of communist regimes in eastern Europe','a fascist regime Mussolini ''s fascist regime in Italy','a democratic regime the establishment of a liberal democratic regime','an oppressive/repressive regime (= powerful, cruel, and unfair ) That country was held fast in the grip of an oppressive regime.','a brutal regime (= cruel and violent ) Many asylum seekers have fled from brutal regimes.','a corrupt regime (= dishonest ) Much of the aid that the Americans sent lined the pockets of his corrupt regime.','overthrow/topple a regime (= remove it from power ) In 1979, Tanzanian forces overthrew the regime of Ugandan dictator Idi Amin.','oppose a regime (= fight or compete against it ) People who opposed the regime were executed in a wave of political violence.','a regime comes to power He criticised European leaders for supporting a regime that came to power through violence.','a regime collapses/falls (= loses power ) Authoritarian regimes tend to collapse in times of economic hardship.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a dietary regime","translation":"یک رژیم غذایی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661867.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('1a1b09a6-5bce-59bd-8768-071cfc1ade97','ae5d9f7e-03ca-5cd8-a70b-e18b18e61998',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a large area of a country or of the world, usually without exact limits',null,null,'ناحیه، منطقه؛ ناحیه (بازی)؛ ناحیه (بدن)',array['area']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"efforts to bring peace to the region","translation":"تلاش برای برقراری صلح در منطقه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661881.mp3"},{"sentence":"the Choco region of Columbia","translation":"منطقه Choco در کلمبیا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001320.mp3"},{"sentence":"Flooding is likely in some coastal regions of the Northeast during the early part of the week.","translation":"احتمال وقوع سیل در برخی از مناطق ساحلی شمال شرق در اوایل هفته وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001321.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('52b16b17-c3b1-5d11-b176-30d8a295d506','ae5d9f7e-03ca-5cd8-a70b-e18b18e61998',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a particular part of someone’s body',null,null,'قسمت خاصی از بدن کسی',array['area']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the lower back region","translation":"ناحیه کمر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000769858.mp3"},{"sentence":"a region of the brain","translation":"یک منطقه از مغز","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001661890.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('9c616059-f867-5ca4-b54c-0d59a8558b33','ae5d9f7e-03ca-5cd8-a70b-e18b18e61998',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'(somewhere) in the region of something','ناحیه، منطقه؛ ناحیه (بازی)؛ ناحیه (بدن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('629ac1af-eb1a-5213-bc3b-0d681fb6d430','ae5d9f7e-03ca-5cd8-a70b-e18b18e61998',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'the regions','ناحیه، منطقه؛ ناحیه (بازی)؛ ناحیه (بدن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('824c8624-4aa9-5bcb-a77e-3a1ddee94f02','f0fbffd0-5b8c-5969-a671-7461d296be1d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to feel sorry about something you have done and wish you had not done it',null,null,'حسرت خوردن؛ متأسف بودن (از)؛ اظهار تأسف','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['deeply/greatly I deeply regretted what had happened.','bitterly (= with a feeling of great sadness ) I bitterly regretted my decision to leave.','sincerely The airline sincerely regrets any delays to passengers.','very much We very much regret that there will be job losses.','instantly/immediately ‘No, ’ she blurted out, instantly regretting her response.','live to regret something (= regret it in the future ) If you don’t go, you may live to regret it.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Don’t do anything you might regret.","translation":"کاری نکنید که ممکن است پشیمان شوید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652337.mp3"},{"sentence":"I regret leaving school so young.","translation":"من پشیمانم که خیلی جوان مدرسه را ترک کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001322.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was beginning to regret that he’d come along.","translation":"کم کم داشت پشیمان می شد که اومده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652338.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('304e72d2-e91d-554c-86e3-4ea91e892b41','f0fbffd0-5b8c-5969-a671-7461d296be1d',2,null,null,'formal','used in official letters or statements when saying that you are sorry or sad about something','[ not in progressive ]',null,'در نامه‌ها یا بیانیه‌های رسمی وقتی می‌گویید از چیزی متاسف یا ناراحت هستید استفاده می‌شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['deeply/greatly I deeply regretted what had happened.','bitterly (= with a feeling of great sadness ) I bitterly regretted my decision to leave.','sincerely The airline sincerely regrets any delays to passengers.','very much We very much regret that there will be job losses.','instantly/immediately ‘No, ’ she blurted out, instantly regretting her response.','live to regret something (= regret it in the future ) If you don’t go, you may live to regret it.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We regret any inconvenience caused to our customers.","translation":"ما از هر گونه ناراحتی ایجاد شده برای مشتریان متاسفیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000770247.mp3"},{"sentence":"I regret that I will be unable to attend.","translation":"متاسفم که نمیتونم شرکت کنم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652346.mp3"},{"sentence":"I regret to inform you that your contract will not be renewed.","translation":"با کمال تاسف به اطلاع شما میرسانم که قرارداد شما تمدید نخواهد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000770256.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('b2c8376b-2a43-50f3-b167-40585fb4e9e3','a59e9263-029b-5316-bb11-31b86381f3ea',1,null,null,'spoken & written','sadness that you feel about something, especially because you wish it had not happened','[ countable usually plural, uncountable ]',null,'غم و اندوهی که در مورد چیزی احساس می کنید، به خصوص به این دلیل که آرزو می کنید ای کاش آن اتفاق نمی افتاد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['great/deep regret I accepted his resignation with great regret.','bitter regret (= when you feel sad and angry ) To the bitter regret of his party, he refused to call an election.','somebody’s biggest regret Her biggest regret was not having children.','somebody’s only regret My only regret is that my parents did not live to see this day.','have regrets I have absolutely no regrets.','express regret The president expressed his regret at the deaths.','a pang/twinge/stab of regret literary (= a sudden short feeling of regret ) Kate watched her go with a pang of regret.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I have no regrets about leaving.","translation":"من از رفتن پشیمان نیستم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000770290.mp3"},{"sentence":"She has already expressed deep regret for what happened.","translation":"او قبلاً از آنچه اتفاق افتاده است ابراز تاسف کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652352.mp3"},{"sentence":"I decided with some regret that it was time to move on.","translation":"با کمی تأسف تصمیم گرفتم که وقت آن رسیده است که ادامه دهم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001769266.mp3"},{"sentence":"It is with great regret that I must decline your offer.","translation":"با کمال تاسف باید پیشنهاد شما را رد کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001769267.mp3"},{"sentence":"I lost touch with her, much to my regret.","translation":"من ارتباطم را با او از دست دادم، بسیار متأسفم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001769273.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('0a4d81d3-c6b9-5424-a85b-3feb5f1d638c','a59e9263-029b-5316-bb11-31b86381f3ea',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'give/send your regrets',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['great/deep regret I accepted his resignation with great regret.','bitter regret (= when you feel sad and angry ) To the bitter regret of his party, he refused to call an election.','somebody’s biggest regret Her biggest regret was not having children.','somebody’s only regret My only regret is that my parents did not live to see this day.','have regrets I have absolutely no regrets.','express regret The president expressed his regret at the deaths.','a pang/twinge/stab of regret literary (= a sudden short feeling of regret ) Kate watched her go with a pang of regret.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('1fe9398e-4ffa-51ae-9679-cabc2066c070','fcb2e235-b3c4-5230-bee1-16fa3d6e844e',1,'offer/suggestion/idea','پیشنهاد/پیشنهاد/ایده','spoken & written','to refuse to accept , believe in, or agree with something',null,null,'رد کردن، رفض کردن (پیشنهاد)؛ مأمور (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['reject something outright (= completely ) He has not rejected the idea outright.','firmly reject The British proposals were firmly rejected by the other EU countries.','flatly reject (= in a firm and definite way ) He flatly rejected the rebel’s demands.','totally reject My client totally rejects the accusations.','categorically/unequivocally reject (= in a definite way, leaving no doubt ) We categorically reject their argument.','unanimously reject (= when all members of a group reject something ) The board unanimously rejected the proposal.','decisively reject (= when most members of a group reject something ) On May 21, the House decisively rejected the president’s proposed budget.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Sarah rejected her brother’s offer of help.","translation":"سارا پیشنهاد کمک برادرش را رد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652579.mp3"},{"sentence":"Gibson rejected the idea as ‘absurd’.","translation":"گیبسون این ایده را رد کرد و آن را «پوچ» خواند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652580.mp3"},{"sentence":"Dexter flatly rejected (= completely rejected ) calls for his resignation.","translation":"دکستر به طور قاطع رد شد (= کاملاً رد شد) استعفای خود را خواستار شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652581.mp3"},{"sentence":"His proposal was rejected outright (= completely rejected ) .","translation":"پیشنهاد او کاملاً رد شد (= کاملاً رد شد).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001876655.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('c9248940-3e2a-57ce-bd45-774c8cf49b11','fcb2e235-b3c4-5230-bee1-16fa3d6e844e',2,'not choose somebody','کسی را انتخاب نکن','spoken & written','to not choose someone for a job , course of study etc',null,null,'عدم انتخاب کسی برای شغل، دوره تحصیلی و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['reject something outright (= completely ) He has not rejected the idea outright.','firmly reject The British proposals were firmly rejected by the other EU countries.','flatly reject (= in a firm and definite way ) He flatly rejected the rebel’s demands.','totally reject My client totally rejects the accusations.','categorically/unequivocally reject (= in a definite way, leaving no doubt ) We categorically reject their argument.','unanimously reject (= when all members of a group reject something ) The board unanimously rejected the proposal.','decisively reject (= when most members of a group reject something ) On May 21, the House decisively rejected the president’s proposed budget.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"It’s obvious why his application was rejected.","translation":"واضح است که چرا درخواست او رد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652587.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('6ff0e9c3-b536-5008-8978-fcf2eb1974ea','fcb2e235-b3c4-5230-bee1-16fa3d6e844e',3,'product','محصول','spoken & written','to throw away something that has just been made, because its quality is not good enough',null,null,'دور انداختن چیزی که به تازگی ساخته شده است، زیرا کیفیت آن به اندازه کافی خوب نیست','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['reject something outright (= completely ) He has not rejected the idea outright.','firmly reject The British proposals were firmly rejected by the other EU countries.','flatly reject (= in a firm and definite way ) He flatly rejected the rebel’s demands.','totally reject My client totally rejects the accusations.','categorically/unequivocally reject (= in a definite way, leaving no doubt ) We categorically reject their argument.','unanimously reject (= when all members of a group reject something ) The board unanimously rejected the proposal.','decisively reject (= when most members of a group reject something ) On May 21, the House decisively rejected the president’s proposed budget.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"If inspectors find a defective can, the batch is rejected.","translation":"اگر بازرسان قوطی معیوب پیدا کنند، دسته رد می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652589.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
