('81cf43de-2ee9-5018-ad3a-ece73e74eb64','49881131-ba23-5762-8793-6333fcf2091e',1,null,null,'spoken & written','money that you receive as payment from the organization you work for, usually paid to you every month',null,null,'حقوق، حقوق ماهانه؛ مزد (سالی)؛ حقوق (کار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['earn/get/receive a salary She’s now earning a good salary as an interpreter.','be on a salary British English (= be earning a salary ) He won’t tell me what salary he’s on.','command a salary formal (= be able to get a particular salary ) Which graduates command the highest salaries?','pay somebody a salary Large companies often pay better salaries.','offer somebody a salary We offer competitive salaries to graduates.','increase somebody’s salary His salary was increased to £80,000 a year.','cut somebody’s salary (= reduce someone’s salary ) They will cut salaries before they cut jobs.','high/good She moved to a job with a higher salary.','low It sounds an interesting job, but the salary is too low.','a six-figure salary (= one over £100,000 or $100,000 ) He’s now a top executive with a six-figure salary.','annual salary His annual salary is $200,000.','monthly salary What''s your monthly salary?','current salary His current salary is just over £30,000 a year.','basic/base salary (= the basic amount that someone is paid ) You get a basic salary, and then other benefits on top.','starting salary (= the salary someone gets when they start a job ) The starting salary for a hotel manager is $26,400.','final salary Your pension is based on a proportion of your final salary.','a salary increase He was given a huge salary increase.','a salary cut (= a decrease in someone’s salary ) The workforce agreed to take salary cuts.','the salary scale/structure (= the list of increasing salaries that someone in a job can earn ) He is almost at the top of his salary scale.','a drop/cut in salary (= a reduction in salary ) He couldn’t afford to take a drop in salary.','an increase/rise in salary They were offered a 10% increase in salary.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The average salary for a teacher is $39,000 a year.","translation":"میانگین حقوق یک معلم 39000 دلار در سال است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001417.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('88c9e94d-4a53-5296-81c7-3cb10cf5cd40','ad845cf4-574a-5e3e-a1a5-4050e96824c2',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a small part or amount of something that is examined in order to find out something about the whole',null,null,'نمونه، عیار (چیز)؛ نمونه (برداشت)؛ نمونه (پیشنهاد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a blood/urine/tissue etc sample He compared the samples with a blood sample from Mr Green.','a water/soil etc sample They analysed soil samples collected from streams.','a DNA sample Archaeologists are studying DNA samples from ancient Egyptian mummies.','take/collect a sample The study took samples from workers at four nuclear plants.','give/provide a sample He said he had once fainted when giving a sample of blood.','analyse/test a sample All the samples were tested for bacteria.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’d like to see some samples of your work.","translation":"من می خواهم چند نمونه از کار شما را ببینم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000742325.mp3"},{"sentence":"They took a blood sample to test for hepatitis.","translation":"برای آزمایش هپاتیت نمونه خون گرفتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000742322.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('408b8940-c69e-5d24-85a4-dae12077bf65','ad845cf4-574a-5e3e-a1a5-4050e96824c2',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a small amount of a product that people can try in order to find out what it is like',null,null,'مقدار کمی از یک محصول که مردم می توانند آن را امتحان کنند تا بفهمند چگونه است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a blood/urine/tissue etc sample He compared the samples with a blood sample from Mr Green.','a water/soil etc sample They analysed soil samples collected from streams.','a DNA sample Archaeologists are studying DNA samples from ancient Egyptian mummies.','take/collect a sample The study took samples from workers at four nuclear plants.','give/provide a sample He said he had once fainted when giving a sample of blood.','analyse/test a sample All the samples were tested for bacteria.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"free samples of a new shampoo","translation":"نمونه رایگان یک شامپوی جدید","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00756.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('9997a0ce-d331-5cfa-9c9b-2403f4ca06d4','ad845cf4-574a-5e3e-a1a5-4050e96824c2',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a small group of people who have been chosen from a larger group to give information or answers to questions',null,null,'گروه کوچکی از افراد که از یک گروه بزرگتر برای دادن اطلاعات یا پاسخ به سوالات انتخاب شده اند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a blood/urine/tissue etc sample He compared the samples with a blood sample from Mr Green.','a water/soil etc sample They analysed soil samples collected from streams.','a DNA sample Archaeologists are studying DNA samples from ancient Egyptian mummies.','take/collect a sample The study took samples from workers at four nuclear plants.','give/provide a sample He said he had once fainted when giving a sample of blood.','analyse/test a sample All the samples were tested for bacteria.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The sample consisted of 98 secondary school teachers.","translation":"نمونه شامل 98 معلم دوره متوسطه بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000742335.mp3"},{"sentence":"Out of a random sample of drivers, 21% had been in an accident in the previous year.","translation":"از یک نمونه تصادفی رانندگان، 21 درصد در سال گذشته تصادف کرده بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000742339.mp3"},{"sentence":"a nationally representative sample of over 950 elderly persons","translation":"نمونه ملی بیش از 950 سالمند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000742343.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('82dce672-e584-5aff-a068-7104aac35f72','ad845cf4-574a-5e3e-a1a5-4050e96824c2',4,null,null,'spoken & written','a small part of a song from a CD or record that is used in a new song',null,null,'بخش کوچکی از یک آهنگ از یک CD یا ضبط که در یک آهنگ جدید استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a blood/urine/tissue etc sample He compared the samples with a blood sample from Mr Green.','a water/soil etc sample They analysed soil samples collected from streams.','a DNA sample Archaeologists are studying DNA samples from ancient Egyptian mummies.','take/collect a sample The study took samples from workers at four nuclear plants.','give/provide a sample He said he had once fainted when giving a sample of blood.','analyse/test a sample All the samples were tested for bacteria.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Her latest album makes extensive use of samples from a wide range of acid jazz tracks.","translation":"آخرین آلبوم او به طور گسترده از نمونه های طیف وسیعی از آهنگ های اسید جاز استفاده می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001810883.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('9dbb1b00-25e3-5e5f-9b72-3b3a4a384245','f6044e75-fe99-5df2-8a93-ae067c386245',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to taste food or drink in order to see what it is like',null,null,'طعم غذا یا نوشیدنی را بچشید تا ببینید چگونه است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a chance to sample the local food","translation":"فرصتی برای امتحان کردن غذاهای محلی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001640577.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('628a1fd3-6021-5380-af72-b45a95c2a259','f6044e75-fe99-5df2-8a93-ae067c386245',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to choose some people from a larger group in order to ask them questions or get information from them',null,null,'چند نفر را از یک گروه بزرگتر انتخاب کنید تا از آنها سوال بپرسید یا از آنها اطلاعات بگیرید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"18% of the adults sampled admitted having had problems with alcohol abuse.","translation":"18 درصد از بزرگسالان نمونه اعتراف کردند که با سوء مصرف الکل مشکل داشتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000742363.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('1cba1cff-19b8-570f-865f-96b23789847a','f6044e75-fe99-5df2-8a93-ae067c386245',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to try an activity , go to a place etc in order to see what it is like',null,null,'برای امتحان کردن یک فعالیت، به یک مکان و غیره بروید تا ببینید چگونه است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Here’s your chance to sample the delights of country life.","translation":"در اینجا شانس شما برای نمونه از لذت های زندگی روستایی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000742367.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('d168552d-e00c-5def-a3a8-7baaa5aa1642','f6044e75-fe99-5df2-8a93-ae067c386245',4,null,null,'spoken & written','to use a small part of a song from a CD or record in a new song',null,null,'برای استفاده از قسمت کوچکی از یک آهنگ از یک CD یا ضبط در یک آهنگ جدید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Many of his songs have been sampled by other artists.","translation":"بسیاری از آهنگ های او توسط هنرمندان دیگر نمونه برداری شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001810891.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('5467df6f-f7ad-5963-9b3e-58ae1ad6ecda','ee0383de-fe4d-539c-bf1d-e9c4bc29d965',1,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'savings','پس‌انداز، پس‌انداز (پول)؛ صرفه‌جویی (مقدار)؛ صرفه (حالت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('bcfdfdc1-409f-56a8-856a-225ccda113d7','ee0383de-fe4d-539c-bf1d-e9c4bc29d965',2,null,null,'spoken & written','an amount of money that you have not spent , or an amount of something that you have not used','[ countable ]',null,'مقدار پولی که خرج نکرده‌اید یا مقداری از چیزی که استفاده نکرده‌اید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The new engines will lead to savings in fuel.","translation":"موتورهای جدید به صرفه جویی در سوخت منجر خواهند شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000715366.mp3"},{"sentence":"This represents a saving of £60,000.","translation":"این نشان دهنده صرفه جویی 60000 پوندی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001610230.mp3"},{"sentence":"All small companies will need to make savings if they are to survive.","translation":"همه شرکت های کوچک برای بقای خود باید پس انداز کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001610231.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('57adedee-9f64-5aef-bd10-07b65dc0bb48','ee0383de-fe4d-539c-bf1d-e9c4bc29d965',3,null,null,'spoken & written','when you save money rather than spend it','[ uncountable ]',null,'وقتی به جای خرج کردن پول پس انداز می کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('3dd2ce72-a938-503b-a970-1a66dee2730a','1014d9cf-7972-598f-b4be-9a9c5f9190ea',1,null,null,'spoken & written','frightened of something, or nervous about something',null,null,'ترسیده، وحشت‌زده (از)',array['afraid']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['very/really scared By this time I was feeling really scared.','quite scared Some of the children were quite scared.','a bit/little scared I was always a little scared of my father.','feel scared She was beginning to feel a bit scared.','look scared What’s the matter? You look scared.','get scared (= start to feel scared ) It was now completely dark and I was getting scared.','scared to death (= extremely scared ) He looked scared to death.','scared stiff informal (= extremely scared ) I was scared stiff of going down those cellar steps.','scared witless/out of your wits informal (= extremely scared ) She admitted she was scared witless.','be running scared (= feel scared, especially because someone might catch you or defeat you ) The opposition were running scared.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"At first, he was really scared.","translation":"اولش واقعا ترسیده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001581599.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’ve always been scared of dogs.","translation":"من همیشه از سگ ها می ترسیدم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000718062.mp3"},{"sentence":"Don’t be scared of asking for help.","translation":"از کمک خواستن نترسید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000718063.mp3"},{"sentence":"I wanted to ask her out, but was scared that she might refuse.","translation":"من می خواستم از او درخواست کنم، اما می ترسیدم که نکند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000718066.mp3"},{"sentence":"The boys were scared to cross the street.","translation":"پسرها از عبور از خیابان می ترسیدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000718069.mp3"},{"sentence":"I was scared stiff at the thought of making a speech.","translation":"از فکر سخنرانی سخت ترسیدم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000718073.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was afraid of losing Anna in the crowd.","translation":"می ترسید آنا را در میان جمعیت از دست بدهد.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,7),
('f4ea7463-f4b2-56d6-bddc-5e49928bd6e4','7662a442-ce63-507d-bb42-9f62c1cf8d8c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an official plan that is intended to help people in some way, for example by providing education or training',null,null,'طرح، نقشه (کمکی)؛ اسکیم (پرداخت)؛ طرح (پیشنهادی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a major scheme The government is introducing a major house-building scheme in the area.','a new scheme The new scheme aims to reduce street crime by 30%.','an innovative scheme (= using new ideas ) an innovative scheme to help the unemployed get back to work','a grand scheme (= trying to achieve a lot ) In the end, the government’s grand scheme came to nothing.','a pilot scheme (= one that is tried on a small scale first to see if it is a good idea ) The programme was introduced into 100 primary schools in a very successful pilot scheme.','a training scheme The company runs an apprentice training scheme.','a pension scheme Does your employer offer a pension scheme?','a compensation/bonus etc scheme (= in which people receive compensation, a bonus etc ) a new compensation scheme for accident victims','an incentive scheme (= in which people receive money to persuade them to work harder ) There is a generous incentive scheme for the sales force.','introduce/launch a scheme The scheme was launched last autumn by the company’s education officer.','run/operate a scheme Parent volunteers help run the scheme.','be covered by a scheme (= be able to benefit from a scheme ) All employees are covered by the new bonus scheme.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The money will be used for teacher training schemes.","translation":"این پول برای طرح های آموزشی معلمان مصرف خواهد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000718889.mp3"},{"sentence":"a pension scheme","translation":"یک طرح بازنشستگی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000718890.mp3"},{"sentence":"schemes for two new cross-city lines","translation":"طرح های دو خط جدید بین شهری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001581779.mp3"},{"sentence":"a new scheme to boost exports","translation":"طرحی جدید برای افزایش صادرات","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001777282.mp3"},{"sentence":"The pilot scheme proved to be a great success.","translation":"طرح آزمایشی موفقیت بزرگی را نشان داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001777285.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('a4d28329-9149-5b8f-824f-7e5d32ad244b','7662a442-ce63-507d-bb42-9f62c1cf8d8c',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a clever plan, especially to do something that is bad or illegal – used to show disapproval',null,null,'یک طرح هوشمندانه، به ویژه برای انجام کاری که بد یا غیرقانونی است - برای نشان دادن عدم تایید استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a major scheme The government is introducing a major house-building scheme in the area.','a new scheme The new scheme aims to reduce street crime by 30%.','an innovative scheme (= using new ideas ) an innovative scheme to help the unemployed get back to work','a grand scheme (= trying to achieve a lot ) In the end, the government’s grand scheme came to nothing.','a pilot scheme (= one that is tried on a small scale first to see if it is a good idea ) The programme was introduced into 100 primary schools in a very successful pilot scheme.','a training scheme The company runs an apprentice training scheme.','a pension scheme Does your employer offer a pension scheme?','a compensation/bonus etc scheme (= in which people receive compensation, a bonus etc ) a new compensation scheme for accident victims','an incentive scheme (= in which people receive money to persuade them to work harder ) There is a generous incentive scheme for the sales force.','introduce/launch a scheme The scheme was launched last autumn by the company’s education officer.','run/operate a scheme Parent volunteers help run the scheme.','be covered by a scheme (= be able to benefit from a scheme ) All employees are covered by the new bonus scheme.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a get-rich-quick scheme","translation":"یک طرح پولدار شدن سریع","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001581780.mp3"},{"sentence":"a scheme to pass false cheques","translation":"طرحی برای پاس کردن چک های نادرست","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001581781.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('0985d73b-90d8-59d4-8c15-ffe8150fa042','7662a442-ce63-507d-bb42-9f62c1cf8d8c',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a system that you use to organize information, ideas etc',null,null,'سیستمی که برای سازماندهی اطلاعات، ایده ها و غیره استفاده می کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a major scheme The government is introducing a major house-building scheme in the area.','a new scheme The new scheme aims to reduce street crime by 30%.','an innovative scheme (= using new ideas ) an innovative scheme to help the unemployed get back to work','a grand scheme (= trying to achieve a lot ) In the end, the government’s grand scheme came to nothing.','a pilot scheme (= one that is tried on a small scale first to see if it is a good idea ) The programme was introduced into 100 primary schools in a very successful pilot scheme.','a training scheme The company runs an apprentice training scheme.','a pension scheme Does your employer offer a pension scheme?','a compensation/bonus etc scheme (= in which people receive compensation, a bonus etc ) a new compensation scheme for accident victims','an incentive scheme (= in which people receive money to persuade them to work harder ) There is a generous incentive scheme for the sales force.','introduce/launch a scheme The scheme was launched last autumn by the company’s education officer.','run/operate a scheme Parent volunteers help run the scheme.','be covered by a scheme (= be able to benefit from a scheme ) All employees are covered by the new bonus scheme.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a classification scheme","translation":"یک طرح طبقه بندی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000718899.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('cdf314dc-85c9-5abc-883b-f799a994f2b6','7662a442-ce63-507d-bb42-9f62c1cf8d8c',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'in the scheme of things','طرح، نقشه (کمکی)؛ اسکیم (پرداخت)؛ طرح (پیشنهادی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a major scheme The government is introducing a major house-building scheme in the area.','a new scheme The new scheme aims to reduce street crime by 30%.','an innovative scheme (= using new ideas ) an innovative scheme to help the unemployed get back to work','a grand scheme (= trying to achieve a lot ) In the end, the government’s grand scheme came to nothing.','a pilot scheme (= one that is tried on a small scale first to see if it is a good idea ) The programme was introduced into 100 primary schools in a very successful pilot scheme.','a training scheme The company runs an apprentice training scheme.','a pension scheme Does your employer offer a pension scheme?','a compensation/bonus etc scheme (= in which people receive compensation, a bonus etc ) a new compensation scheme for accident victims','an incentive scheme (= in which people receive money to persuade them to work harder ) There is a generous incentive scheme for the sales force.','introduce/launch a scheme The scheme was launched last autumn by the company’s education officer.','run/operate a scheme Parent volunteers help run the scheme.','be covered by a scheme (= be able to benefit from a scheme ) All employees are covered by the new bonus scheme.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('2c66c3e6-cc4c-56af-bc2f-ff11813e6e4e','97a5db0d-f585-50b9-9ee1-e4856402fa29',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to secretly make clever and dishonest plans to get or achieve something',null,null,'مخفیانه برای به دست آوردن یا رسیدن به چیزی برنامه ریزی های هوشمندانه و ناصادقانه انجام دادن',array['plot']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She schemed to kill him with poison.","translation":"نقشه کشیده بود که او را با زهر بکشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000718920.mp3"},{"sentence":"He became aware that people were scheming against him and called an emergency meeting.","translation":"او متوجه شد که مردم علیه او مکر می کنند و تشکیل جلسه اضطراری داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000718923.mp3"},{"sentence":"She’s nothing but a lying, scheming little monster!","translation":"او چیزی نیست جز یک هیولای کوچک دروغگو و مکر!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001581793.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('29cfc29a-ff5e-5797-99a7-9cafe6e7d221','09edd4cd-1db2-5540-aa52-3069d2af7b90',1,'where children learn','جایی که بچه ها یاد می گیرند','spoken & written','a place where children are taught','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'مدرسه، مکتب؛ آموزشگاه (دروس)؛ رده (ماهی)؛ رسته (نقاشی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['go to school Did you go to school in Paris?','attend (a) school formal (= go to a school ) Some of the children had not attended school very regularly before.','start school Children in Britain start school when they are five.','leave school He left school when he was 16.','send somebody to school His parents sent him to a private school.','a state school British English , a public school American English (= a school that gets its money from the government ) Universities want to encourage more applicants from state schools.','a private school ( also a public school British English ) (= a school where students pay to study ) He was educated at a private school.','somebody’s old school (= the school someone went to when they were young ) He went back to his old school to give a talk to the children.','a local school (= a school near where someone lives ) They sent their kids to the local school.','a boarding school (= a school where children also live and sleep )','a day school (= a school where children go during the day but go home in the evenings ) The school is both a boarding school and a day school.','a nursery school (= for children under 5 )','an infant school British English (= for children aged 5 to 7 )','a primary school British English , an elementary school American English (= for children up to 11 ) Their children are still at primary school.','a secondary school ( also a high school British English ) (= for children from 11 to 16 or 18 )','a high school American English (= a school for students aged 14 to 18 )','a comprehensive school British English (= a secondary school for all children )','a grammar school British English (= a secondary school for children who have passed an exam when they are 11 )','school students ( also school pupils British English ) Most school students have musical interests of some kind.','a school friend She met some old school friends.','a school uniform He was still wearing his school uniform.','the school holidays British English The trip will take place during the school holidays.','the school run British English (= the journey taking children to and from school each day ) She had to be back in time for the school run.','the school playground','the school library','the school hall','the school bus','the school curriculum Head teachers were asked to incorporate road safety education in the school curriculum.','school meals/lunches ( also school dinners British English ) We provide good-quality school meals.','a school governor British English (= an elected person who works with teachers to make decisions about how a school is organized ) The school governors have appointed a new head teacher.','the school board American English (= the group of people who are elected to govern a school or group of schools ) The courts have upheld the school board''s right to dismiss striking teachers.','the school day Most children are tired at the end of the school day.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"His mother always used to pick him up from school.","translation":"مادرش همیشه او را از مدرسه می برد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001919005.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('318f1b20-b83f-5562-a00f-cca1e543d513','09edd4cd-1db2-5540-aa52-3069d2af7b90',2,'time at school','زمان در مدرسه','spoken & written','a day’s work at school','[ uncountable ]',null,'یک روز کار در مدرسه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['go to school Did you go to school in Paris?','attend (a) school formal (= go to a school ) Some of the children had not attended school very regularly before.','start school Children in Britain start school when they are five.','leave school He left school when he was 16.','send somebody to school His parents sent him to a private school.','a state school British English , a public school American English (= a school that gets its money from the government ) Universities want to encourage more applicants from state schools.','a private school ( also a public school British English ) (= a school where students pay to study ) He was educated at a private school.','somebody’s old school (= the school someone went to when they were young ) He went back to his old school to give a talk to the children.','a local school (= a school near where someone lives ) They sent their kids to the local school.','a boarding school (= a school where children also live and sleep )','a day school (= a school where children go during the day but go home in the evenings ) The school is both a boarding school and a day school.','a nursery school (= for children under 5 )','an infant school British English (= for children aged 5 to 7 )','a primary school British English , an elementary school American English (= for children up to 11 ) Their children are still at primary school.','a secondary school ( also a high school British English ) (= for children from 11 to 16 or 18 )','a high school American English (= a school for students aged 14 to 18 )','a comprehensive school British English (= a secondary school for all children )','a grammar school British English (= a secondary school for children who have passed an exam when they are 11 )','school students ( also school pupils British English ) Most school students have musical interests of some kind.','a school friend She met some old school friends.','a school uniform He was still wearing his school uniform.','the school holidays British English The trip will take place during the school holidays.','the school run British English (= the journey taking children to and from school each day ) She had to be back in time for the school run.','the school playground','the school library','the school hall','the school bus','the school curriculum Head teachers were asked to incorporate road safety education in the school curriculum.','school meals/lunches ( also school dinners British English ) We provide good-quality school meals.','a school governor British English (= an elected person who works with teachers to make decisions about how a school is organized ) The school governors have appointed a new head teacher.','the school board American English (= the group of people who are elected to govern a school or group of schools ) The courts have upheld the school board''s right to dismiss striking teachers.','the school day Most children are tired at the end of the school day.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"School begins at 8.30.","translation":"شروع مدرسه ساعت 8.30","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000719260.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’ll see you after school.","translation":"بعد از مدرسه می بینمت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000719263.mp3"},{"sentence":"He’s one of my old friends from school.","translation":"او یکی از دوستان قدیمی من در مدرسه است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000719267.mp3"},{"sentence":"Children start school between the ages of four and five.","translation":"بچه ها از سن چهار تا پنج سالگی مدرسه را شروع می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001428.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('b2373c0a-6d04-55ed-963e-920ddc34799c','09edd4cd-1db2-5540-aa52-3069d2af7b90',3,'university','دانشگاه','spoken & written','a college or university , or the time when you study there','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'یک کالج یا دانشگاه، یا زمانی که در آنجا تحصیل می کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Their kids are away at school now.","translation":"بچه هایشان الان در مدرسه نیستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000719279.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was going to school in Boston.","translation":"او در بوستون به مدرسه می رفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001429.mp3"},{"sentence":"the Harvard School of Public Health","translation":"دانشکده بهداشت عمومی هاروارد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000719289.mp3"},{"sentence":"After two years of medical school, I thought I knew everything.","translation":"بعد از دو سال دانشکده پزشکی، فکر کردم همه چیز را می دانم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000719282.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
