secrets with him.','a family secret Their normally strong relationship is threatened when he has to reveal a family secret.','a state/official secret (= a government secret ) He was accused of passing on state secrets to a foreign power.','a trade secret (= a company or business secret ) They must not betray their employer’s trust, for instance by giving away trade secrets.','military secrets He was sent to prison for five years in 1933 for selling military secrets to Germany.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
