('eb81538f-84e5-5a9a-949f-d41a147098fb','7cff0d50-a53f-5b88-b651-5ea6d3e61fd7',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'make no secret of something','راز، سر؛ راز (خانه)؛ راز (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a secret We have no secrets from each other.','know a secret (= about someone else ) You can tell Tom that I know his secret.','keep a secret (= not tell it to anyone ) Can you keep a secret?','tell somebody a secret Shall I tell you a secret?','let somebody in on a secret (= tell them a secret ) Frank let me in on the secret.','reveal/divulge a secret formal (= tell it to someone ) He was accused of revealing state secrets.','give away a secret (= tell it to someone carelessly or by mistake ) I had to be careful not to give away any secrets.','share a secret (= tell it to someone because you trust them ) I trusted Alexander, so I decided to share my secret with him.','discover/find out a secret He was afraid that someone would discover his secret.','a big secret (= an important secret or one that very few people know ) The event was supposed to be a big secret, but everyone knew about it.','a little secret (= a personal secret that very few people know ) You must promise me that this will be our little secret.','a closely-guarded/well-kept secret (= a secret that few people are allowed to know ) The recipe is a closely-guarded secret.','an open secret (= something that a lot of people know, but do not talk about because it is supposed to be a secret ) It was an open secret that he was having an affair.','a dark/terrible secret (= a secret about something bad ) I’m sure every family has a few dark secrets.','a dirty secret (= a shameful secret ) The exclusion of black people from the film industry is one of Hollywood’s dirty little secrets.','a guilty secret (= a secret that someone feels guilty about ) He had finally discovered Jo’s guilty secret.','somebody’s innermost secrets (= very private or personal secrets ) She wasn’t confident enough to share her innermost secrets with him.','a family secret Their normally strong relationship is threatened when he has to reveal a family secret.','a state/official secret (= a government secret ) He was accused of passing on state secrets to a foreign power.','a trade secret (= a company or business secret ) They must not betray their employer’s trust, for instance by giving away trade secrets.','military secrets He was sent to prison for five years in 1933 for selling military secrets to Germany.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('28032f48-f017-58af-a943-80acbe9079ea','7cff0d50-a53f-5b88-b651-5ea6d3e61fd7',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'the secrets of life/nature/the universe etc','راز، سر؛ راز (خانه)؛ راز (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a secret We have no secrets from each other.','know a secret (= about someone else ) You can tell Tom that I know his secret.','keep a secret (= not tell it to anyone ) Can you keep a secret?','tell somebody a secret Shall I tell you a secret?','let somebody in on a secret (= tell them a secret ) Frank let me in on the secret.','reveal/divulge a secret formal (= tell it to someone ) He was accused of revealing state secrets.','give away a secret (= tell it to someone carelessly or by mistake ) I had to be careful not to give away any secrets.','share a secret (= tell it to someone because you trust them ) I trusted Alexander, so I decided to share my secret with him.','discover/find out a secret He was afraid that someone would discover his secret.','a big secret (= an important secret or one that very few people know ) The event was supposed to be a big secret, but everyone knew about it.','a little secret (= a personal secret that very few people know ) You must promise me that this will be our little secret.','a closely-guarded/well-kept secret (= a secret that few people are allowed to know ) The recipe is a closely-guarded secret.','an open secret (= something that a lot of people know, but do not talk about because it is supposed to be a secret ) It was an open secret that he was having an affair.','a dark/terrible secret (= a secret about something bad ) I’m sure every family has a few dark secrets.','a dirty secret (= a shameful secret ) The exclusion of black people from the film industry is one of Hollywood’s dirty little secrets.','a guilty secret (= a secret that someone feels guilty about ) He had finally discovered Jo’s guilty secret.','somebody’s innermost secrets (= very private or personal secrets ) She wasn’t confident enough to share her innermost secrets with him.','a family secret Their normally strong relationship is threatened when he has to reveal a family secret.','a state/official secret (= a government secret ) He was accused of passing on state secrets to a foreign power.','a trade secret (= a company or business secret ) They must not betray their employer’s trust, for instance by giving away trade secrets.','military secrets He was sent to prison for five years in 1933 for selling military secrets to Germany.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('f761e0f2-3abc-5213-978d-397966c2373d','047f8bab-ae05-5e78-8c52-e5ec22dc3e8b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a part of an area of activity , especially of business, trade etc',null,null,'بخش، قطب (اقتصاد)؛ بخش (کشور)؛ بخش (صنعت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an economic sector (= one part of the economy ) The country is making efforts to expand such economic sectors as tourism and information technology.','the agricultural/manufacturing/industrial sector (= the part of the economy to do with growing food/producing goods ) As the industrial sector grew, more and more of the population moved to the cities.','the service sector (= the part of the economy to do with providing services, such as banking or tourism ) The proportion of service sector jobs within the economy has grown.','the financial/banking sector (= the part of the economy to do with money and finance ) The UK financial sector is looking healthier than ever.','the public sector (= businesses controlled by the government ) The government has been holding down pay in the public sector.','the private sector (= businesses that the government does not control ) Generally speaking, employees in the private sector are well rewarded.','the voluntary sector (= people doing socially useful work for no money ) The voluntary sector has an important role in tackling urban deprivation.','an important sector Sport is now recognized as an important sector of economic activity.','a key sector (= a very important one ) They identified cars and electronics as key sectors in the economy.','the rented sector (= homes that people can rent ) We have lost 2 million homes from the rented sector.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the agricultural sector of the economy","translation":"بخش کشاورزی اقتصاد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000725928.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('8a17d3a5-926e-5f72-9c37-d2d15516d9f5','047f8bab-ae05-5e78-8c52-e5ec22dc3e8b',2,null,null,'spoken & written','one of the parts into which an area is divided , especially for military purposes',null,null,'یکی از قسمت هایی که یک منطقه به ویژه برای اهداف نظامی به آن تقسیم می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an economic sector (= one part of the economy ) The country is making efforts to expand such economic sectors as tourism and information technology.','the agricultural/manufacturing/industrial sector (= the part of the economy to do with growing food/producing goods ) As the industrial sector grew, more and more of the population moved to the cities.','the service sector (= the part of the economy to do with providing services, such as banking or tourism ) The proportion of service sector jobs within the economy has grown.','the financial/banking sector (= the part of the economy to do with money and finance ) The UK financial sector is looking healthier than ever.','the public sector (= businesses controlled by the government ) The government has been holding down pay in the public sector.','the private sector (= businesses that the government does not control ) Generally speaking, employees in the private sector are well rewarded.','the voluntary sector (= people doing socially useful work for no money ) The voluntary sector has an important role in tackling urban deprivation.','an important sector Sport is now recognized as an important sector of economic activity.','a key sector (= a very important one ) They identified cars and electronics as key sectors in the economy.','the rented sector (= homes that people can rent ) We have lost 2 million homes from the rented sector.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('19015ecb-5e83-552b-8191-b362f382a999','d224b32a-4d6a-5a25-96a8-585793588390',1,'get/achieve','بدست آوردن/دستیابی','spoken & written','to get or achieve something that will be permanent , especially after a lot of effort',null,null,'دست یافتن، تثبیت کردن (پست)؛ محکم کردن (در)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Boyd’s goal secured his team’s place in the Cup Final.","translation":"گل بوید حضور تیمش در فینال جام حذفی را تضمین کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564623.mp3"},{"sentence":"The company secured a $20 million contract.","translation":"این شرکت قراردادی 20 میلیون دلاری منعقد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564631.mp3"},{"sentence":"Negotiators are still working to secure the hostages’ release.","translation":"مذاکره کنندگان همچنان برای آزادی گروگان ها تلاش می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564632.mp3"},{"sentence":"Redgrave won his third Olympic gold medal, and secured his place in history .","translation":"ردگریو سومین مدال طلای المپیک خود را به دست آورد و جایگاه خود را در تاریخ تثبیت کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564638.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('b4475dff-0b4d-543b-b74c-e2fac3d6cdb7','d224b32a-4d6a-5a25-96a8-585793588390',2,'safe from harm','در امان از آسیب','spoken & written','to make something safe from being attacked, harmed , or lost',null,null,'برای ایمن کردن چیزی از حمله، آسیب یا گم شدن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Troops were sent to secure the border.","translation":"نیروها برای تامین امنیت مرز اعزام شدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564645.mp3"},{"sentence":"They built a ten-foot high fence to secure the house against intruders.","translation":"آنها حصاری به ارتفاع ده فوت ساختند تا خانه را در برابر مزاحمان حفظ کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040205.mp3"},{"sentence":"an agreement to secure the future of the rainforest","translation":"توافقی برای تضمین آینده جنگل های بارانی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564646.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('a59d1edf-2979-5c7a-b857-c821b1516f12','d224b32a-4d6a-5a25-96a8-585793588390',3,'tie firmly','محکم ببند','spoken & written','to fasten or tie something firmly in a particular position',null,null,'محکم بستن یا محکم بستن چیزی در موقعیتی خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"John secured the boat firmly to the jetty.","translation":"جان قایق را محکم روی اسکله محکم کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000726028.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('72f5ab8a-e9a0-5b7a-a1b4-4fae0049e24a','d224b32a-4d6a-5a25-96a8-585793588390',4,'borrowing money','قرض گرفتن پول','spoken & written','if you secure a debt or a loan , you legally promise that, if you cannot pay back the money you have borrowed , you will give the lender goods or property of the same value instead',null,null,'اگر قرض یا وامی را تضمین کنید، قانوناً قول می‌دهید که اگر نتوانید پولی را که قرض گرفته‌اید بازپرداخت کنید، به جای آن کالاها یا اموالی را به همان ارزش به وام دهنده می‌دهید.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He used his house to secure the loan .","translation":"او از خانه اش برای تامین وام استفاده کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000726032.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('83c15894-7bce-50c5-806e-22767a8f3221','609e75f2-38da-51c3-bd98-52a6cbba91ca',1,'permanent/certain','دائمی/معین','spoken & written','a situation that is secure is one that you can depend on because it is not likely to change',null,null,'پایدار، مطمئن؛ استوار (شغل)؛ مقاوم (قفل)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"There are no secure jobs these days.","translation":"این روزها هیچ شغل مطمئنی وجود ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564659.mp3"},{"sentence":"We want a secure future for our children.","translation":"ما آینده ای مطمئن برای فرزندانمان می خواهیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564663.mp3"},{"sentence":"United’s position at the top of the league seems relatively secure.","translation":"موقعیت یونایتد در صدر لیگ نسبتا امن به نظر می رسد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564667.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('ad0a31ec-a090-59ff-8627-839612b63738','609e75f2-38da-51c3-bd98-52a6cbba91ca',2,'place/building','مکان/ساختمان','spoken & written','locked or guarded so that people cannot get in or out or steal anything',null,null,'قفل یا محافظت می شود تا مردم نتوانند وارد یا خارج شوند یا چیزی را سرقت کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The house isn’t very secure – we need some new locks.","translation":"خانه خیلی امن نیست - ما به چند قفل جدید نیاز داریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000726053.mp3"},{"sentence":"Keep your passport in a secure place .","translation":"پاسپورت خود را در مکانی امن نگهداری کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564671.mp3"},{"sentence":"In the last year, only three children under the age of 14 have had to be placed in secure accommodation.","translation":"در سال گذشته، تنها سه کودک زیر 14 سال باید در محل اقامت امن قرار می گرفتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001773539.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('82aa71e6-f225-5f34-96ee-c86c9c886155','609e75f2-38da-51c3-bd98-52a6cbba91ca',3,'safe from harm','در امان از آسیب','spoken & written','safe from and protected against damage or attack',null,null,'ایمن و در برابر آسیب یا حمله محافظت می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Companies can offer secure credit card transactions over the Internet.","translation":"شرکت ها می توانند تراکنش های امن با کارت اعتباری را از طریق اینترنت ارائه دهند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564682.mp3"},{"sentence":"These elephants are relatively secure from poachers.","translation":"این فیل ها از شکارچیان غیرقانونی نسبتاً ایمن هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564685.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('8f1f4038-8992-51b9-8bb7-0714b2da86a5','609e75f2-38da-51c3-bd98-52a6cbba91ca',4,'confident','مطمئن','spoken & written','feeling confident about yourself and your abilities',null,null,'احساس اطمینان نسبت به خود و توانایی های خود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We want our children to be secure and feel good about themselves.","translation":"ما می خواهیم فرزندانمان امنیت داشته باشند و نسبت به خودشان احساس خوبی داشته باشند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000726070.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('1dc99a54-7269-5150-bfd1-fe16796718c4','609e75f2-38da-51c3-bd98-52a6cbba91ca',5,'not worried','نگران نیست','spoken & written','feeling confident and certain about a situation and not worried that it might change',null,null,'احساس اطمینان و اطمینان در مورد یک موقعیت و عدم نگرانی از تغییر آن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Workers no longer feel secure about the future.","translation":"کارگران دیگر نسبت به آینده احساس امنیت نمی کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564691.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was enough money to make us feel financially secure .","translation":"این پول کافی بود تا از نظر مالی احساس امنیت کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564695.mp3"},{"sentence":"We huddled together, secure in the knowledge that the rescue helicopter was on its way.","translation":"ما دور هم جمع شدیم و مطمئن بودیم که هلیکوپتر نجات در راه است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564699.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('df2d3a07-cef1-50d8-8423-b70af79f4df0','609e75f2-38da-51c3-bd98-52a6cbba91ca',6,'firmly fastened','محکم بسته شده','spoken & written','firmly fastened or tied, and not likely to fall down',null,null,'محکم بسته یا گره خورده است و احتمال سقوط ندارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Are you sure that shelf is secure?","translation":"آیا مطمئن هستید که قفسه امن است؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000726087.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('cf0fb20d-bb1c-5235-90df-35318c7dae36','2ad2bfdd-6d9d-50b7-9577-311e4bf44afa',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to choose something or someone by thinking carefully about which is the best, most suitable etc',null,null,'انتخاب کردن، گزینش کردن (با دقت)',array['choose','pick']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a group of students selected at random","translation":"گروهی از دانش آموزان به صورت تصادفی انتخاب شدند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001982913.mp3"},{"sentence":"He had hopes of being selected for the national team.","translation":"او به انتخاب تیم ملی امیدوار بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001576186.mp3"},{"sentence":"York was selected as the site for the research centre.","translation":"یورک به عنوان سایت مرکز تحقیقات انتخاب شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001576189.mp3"},{"sentence":"They selected the winner from six finalists.","translation":"آنها برنده را از بین شش فینالیست انتخاب کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001576192.mp3"},{"sentence":"Simon’s been selected to go to the conference.","translation":"سیمون برای رفتن به کنفرانس انتخاب شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000694259.mp3"},{"sentence":"They chose the winner from six finalists.","translation":"آنها از بین شش فینالیست برنده را انتخاب کردند.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,6),
('ced2a760-843d-524f-8cb8-ded79cb83a92','372118b7-02a9-5fba-a14f-1471ccde8d8e',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a select group of people or things is a small special group that has been chosen carefully',null,null,'یک گروه منتخب از افراد یا چیزها یک گروه کوچک خاص است که با دقت انتخاب شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The party was small and select.","translation":"مهمانی کوچک و منتخب بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000694269.mp3"},{"sentence":"Honorary degrees are handed out to a select few .","translation":"مدارک افتخاری به تعداد معدودی اعطا می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001576195.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('91f07408-4d26-5044-9a34-fe19af6c3441','372118b7-02a9-5fba-a14f-1471ccde8d8e',2,null,null,'spoken & written','only lived in, visited, or used by a small number of rich people',null,null,'فقط تعداد کمی از افراد ثروتمند در آن زندگی می کردند، بازدید می کردند یا استفاده می کردند',array['exclusive']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a select block of flats","translation":"یک بلوک آپارتمانی منتخب","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000694279.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('2d27dc2b-6103-5dc7-a902-347b8eabd553','d6df825b-2a54-51f9-a778-eaa7d7903d30',1,null,null,'spoken & written','having a higher position , level , or rank',null,null,'ارشد، بالاتر (رتبه)؛ ارشد (مدرسه)؛ سنین (بالای)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['senior management Within the week senior management approved her proposal.','senior staff Some senior staff criticized the headteacher''s behaviour.','a senior manager She''s now a senior manager for a large toy company.','a senior executive (= in a company ) All the company''s senior executives get large bonuses.','a senior official (= in an organization ) a meeting of senior government officials','a senior officer (= in the police or military ) Inspector Wild is the senior officer in charge of the investigation.','a senior partner (= in a law firm etc ) He was a senior partner in a prestigious Canadian law firm.','a senior member The president announced a reshuffle involving several senior members of his Cabinet.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the senior Democrat on the House committee","translation":"دموکرات ارشد کمیته مجلس نمایندگان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635223.mp3"},{"sentence":"White men hold most of the jobs in senior management .","translation":"مردان سفید پوست بیشتر مشاغل مدیریت ارشد را دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000700397.mp3"},{"sentence":"the senior partner in a law firm","translation":"شریک ارشد در یک شرکت حقوقی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635227.mp3"},{"sentence":"He is also a diplomat, but senior to me.","translation":"او هم دیپلمات است، اما از من ارشد است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000700400.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('f3f39b84-ea4a-5c18-869b-f50b956cf254','d6df825b-2a54-51f9-a778-eaa7d7903d30',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a senior competition is for older people or for people at a more advanced level','[ only before noun ]',null,'مسابقه بزرگسالان برای افراد مسن یا برای افراد در سطح پیشرفته تر است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['senior management Within the week senior management approved her proposal.','senior staff Some senior staff criticized the headteacher''s behaviour.','a senior manager She''s now a senior manager for a large toy company.','a senior executive (= in a company ) All the company''s senior executives get large bonuses.','a senior official (= in an organization ) a meeting of senior government officials','a senior officer (= in the police or military ) Inspector Wild is the senior officer in charge of the investigation.','a senior partner (= in a law firm etc ) He was a senior partner in a prestigious Canadian law firm.','a senior member The president announced a reshuffle involving several senior members of his Cabinet.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I won the 60-metre race, my first senior success.","translation":"من در مسابقه 60 متر برنده شدم، اولین موفقیت من در بزرگسالان.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635232.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
