('5789f7e4-3dd9-531b-9aed-bb432cee5c06','62e82a69-a862-5fb5-bbda-fe36552dfde6',1,null,null,'spoken & written','if goods are sourced from a particular place, they are obtained from that place',null,null,'اگر کالا از یک مکان خاص تهیه شده باشد، از آن مکان تهیه می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Fish for the restaurant is sourced daily from British ports.","translation":"ماهی برای رستوران روزانه از بنادر بریتانیا تهیه می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001606652.mp3"},{"sentence":"locally sourced milk","translation":"شیر محلی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001606653.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('43122cca-0f8e-5a50-8940-5c1e4aa79e23','62e82a69-a862-5fb5-bbda-fe36552dfde6',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to find out where something can be obtained',null,null,'برای پیدا کردن جایی که می توان چیزی به دست آورد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We might be able to source the parts.","translation":"شاید بتوانیم قطعات را تهیه کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001606654.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('99576c16-5140-5670-a50d-d7f6bd56c634','3ddb9bd4-ba38-50a4-96c2-0082eaac0333',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a talk, especially a formal one about a particular subject , given to a group of people','[ countable ]',null,'سخنرانی، نطق؛ بیان (زبان)؛ نطق (مجلس)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['give/make a speech She gave a speech at the party conference.','deliver a speech formal The president delivered a major speech to Congress yesterday.','long The speeches were all really long.','short/brief The chairman opened the meeting with a brief speech.','a passionate/impassioned speech (= full of strong feeling ) She made impassioned speeches on civil rights.','an emotional speech (= showing emotions, especially by crying ) On retiring, she delivered an emotional farewell speech.','a moving speech (= making people feel strong emotions ) That was a very moving speech.','a powerful speech (= having a strong effect on people’s opinions ) He gave a powerful speech calling for unity.','a rousing/stirring speech (= making people feel excited and eager to do something ) Thousands of people were inspired by his stirring speeches.','a major speech (= very important ) This was her first major speech as party leader.','somebody’s inaugural speech (= their first one in an important political job ) He said all the right things in his inaugural speech.','somebody’s acceptance speech (= when they accept a political job, a prize, or an award ) In his acceptance speech, he paid tribute to his wife.','a farewell speech (= by someone who is leaving )','an after-dinner speech (= after a formal dinner ) He gets paid a lot for making after-dinner speeches.','a keynote speech (= the most important one at an event ) The prime minister will make his keynote speech at the conference today.','a political speech She began writing political speeches for local politicians.','a campaign speech (= given during a political campaign ) Eisenhower was careful in his campaign speeches to use only the vaguest of phrases.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Each child had to give a short speech to the rest of the class.","translation":"هر کودک باید برای بقیه کلاس سخنرانی کوتاهی می کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000656151.mp3"},{"sentence":"He has to make a lot of after-dinner speeches .","translation":"او مجبور است بعد از شام سخنرانی های زیادی داشته باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040232.mp3"},{"sentence":"a major speech on relations with China","translation":"سخنرانی بزرگ در مورد روابط با چین","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001623637.mp3"},{"sentence":"Collins gave the keynote speech (= most important speech ) .","translation":"کالینز سخنرانی اصلی را انجام داد (= مهمترین سخنرانی).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001623641.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('cc8e9e44-024a-54c8-9f7f-e063c033743f','3ddb9bd4-ba38-50a4-96c2-0082eaac0333',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the ability to speak','[ uncountable ]',null,'توانایی صحبت کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['give/make a speech She gave a speech at the party conference.','deliver a speech formal The president delivered a major speech to Congress yesterday.','long The speeches were all really long.','short/brief The chairman opened the meeting with a brief speech.','a passionate/impassioned speech (= full of strong feeling ) She made impassioned speeches on civil rights.','an emotional speech (= showing emotions, especially by crying ) On retiring, she delivered an emotional farewell speech.','a moving speech (= making people feel strong emotions ) That was a very moving speech.','a powerful speech (= having a strong effect on people’s opinions ) He gave a powerful speech calling for unity.','a rousing/stirring speech (= making people feel excited and eager to do something ) Thousands of people were inspired by his stirring speeches.','a major speech (= very important ) This was her first major speech as party leader.','somebody’s inaugural speech (= their first one in an important political job ) He said all the right things in his inaugural speech.','somebody’s acceptance speech (= when they accept a political job, a prize, or an award ) In his acceptance speech, he paid tribute to his wife.','a farewell speech (= by someone who is leaving )','an after-dinner speech (= after a formal dinner ) He gets paid a lot for making after-dinner speeches.','a keynote speech (= the most important one at an event ) The prime minister will make his keynote speech at the conference today.','a political speech She began writing political speeches for local politicians.','a campaign speech (= given during a political campaign ) Eisenhower was careful in his campaign speeches to use only the vaguest of phrases.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Only humans are capable of speech.","translation":"فقط انسانها قادر به تکلم هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000656156.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
