('3100e781-234a-5397-9a2a-bd15982552aa','0784ee4c-7d71-5d1f-ad2c-11659bd5988b',2,null,null,'spoken & written','your social or professional rank or position, considered in relation to other people','[ uncountable ]',null,'رتبه یا موقعیت اجتماعی یا حرفه ای شما، در ارتباط با افراد دیگر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['high status They were men of high status and great influence.','low status People who work as carers have low status in our society.','higher/superior status Landowners had superior status.','lower/inferior status In parts of the world, women still have inferior status.','exalted status formal (= very high ) They looked entirely at ease with their exalted status.','equal status Workers of equal status should be rewarded equally.','social status I lied about my family’s social status.','socioeconomic status formal (= relating to your social rank and money ) migrant farm workers and others of low socioeconomic status','professional status His ambition was to attain the highest professional status.','have high/low status ( also enjoy high/low status ) Here, old people are respected and have high social status.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"low-status jobs","translation":"مشاغل با موقعیت پایین","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000641088.mp3"},{"sentence":"Doctors have traditionally enjoyed high social status .","translation":"پزشکان به طور سنتی از موقعیت اجتماعی بالایی برخوردار بوده اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652267.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
