('c35b0424-1e1c-5890-89a6-327e9608ac47','e7a3140c-a0c2-52ae-96c5-8f956597e2b1',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to try to deal with a difficult problem','[ transitive ]',null,'مقابله کردن، رسیدگی کردن (به مشکل)؛ کنترل کردن (توپ)؛ حمله کردن (فوتبال)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['tackle a problem/issue/question The government has failed to tackle the problem of youth crime.','tackle a job/challenge She said she couldn’t face tackling the job on her own.','tackle a blaze/fire (= try to stop it ) Fire crews tackling the blaze were hampered by exploding gas canisters.','tackle crime The police set up a special task force to tackle street crime in the capital.','tackle poverty He believes education is the long-term key to tackling poverty.','tackle unemployment The government announced a new initiative to tackle unemployment.','tackle something head-on (= in a direct and determined way ) The issue of cost must be tackled head-on.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There is more than one way to tackle the problem.","translation":"بیش از یک راه برای مقابله با مشکل وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001622251.mp3"},{"sentence":"It took twelve fire engines to tackle the blaze .","translation":"12 ماشین آتش نشانی برای مهار آتش نیاز داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000609114.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('64028869-9056-55df-872b-6919e91b52c2','e7a3140c-a0c2-52ae-96c5-8f956597e2b1',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to try to take the ball away from an opponent in a game such as football or hockey','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'تلاش برای گرفتن توپ از حریف در یک بازی مانند فوتبال یا هاکی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['tackle a problem/issue/question The government has failed to tackle the problem of youth crime.','tackle a job/challenge She said she couldn’t face tackling the job on her own.','tackle a blaze/fire (= try to stop it ) Fire crews tackling the blaze were hampered by exploding gas canisters.','tackle crime The police set up a special task force to tackle street crime in the capital.','tackle poverty He believes education is the long-term key to tackling poverty.','tackle unemployment The government announced a new initiative to tackle unemployment.','tackle something head-on (= in a direct and determined way ) The issue of cost must be tackled head-on.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('2dfb0392-a6ea-5d77-a65d-04245b1f9954','e7a3140c-a0c2-52ae-96c5-8f956597e2b1',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to talk to someone in order to deal with a difficult problem','[ transitive ]',null,'صحبت کردن با کسی برای مقابله با یک مشکل دشوار','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['tackle a problem/issue/question The government has failed to tackle the problem of youth crime.','tackle a job/challenge She said she couldn’t face tackling the job on her own.','tackle a blaze/fire (= try to stop it ) Fire crews tackling the blaze were hampered by exploding gas canisters.','tackle crime The police set up a special task force to tackle street crime in the capital.','tackle poverty He believes education is the long-term key to tackling poverty.','tackle unemployment The government announced a new initiative to tackle unemployment.','tackle something head-on (= in a direct and determined way ) The issue of cost must be tackled head-on.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"When I tackled Susan about it, she admitted she’d made a mistake.","translation":"وقتی با سوزان در مورد آن صحبت کردم، او اعتراف کرد که اشتباه کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000609121.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ea24c8fb-efe7-5081-908d-4602917ebf77','e7a3140c-a0c2-52ae-96c5-8f956597e2b1',4,null,null,'spoken & written','to start fighting someone, especially a criminal','[ transitive ]',null,'شروع به مبارزه با کسی، به خصوص یک جنایتکار','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['tackle a problem/issue/question The government has failed to tackle the problem of youth crime.','tackle a job/challenge She said she couldn’t face tackling the job on her own.','tackle a blaze/fire (= try to stop it ) Fire crews tackling the blaze were hampered by exploding gas canisters.','tackle crime The police set up a special task force to tackle street crime in the capital.','tackle poverty He believes education is the long-term key to tackling poverty.','tackle unemployment The government announced a new initiative to tackle unemployment.','tackle something head-on (= in a direct and determined way ) The issue of cost must be tackled head-on.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I certainly couldn’t tackle both of them on my own.","translation":"من مطمئناً نمی توانستم به تنهایی با هر دوی آنها مقابله کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000609144.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('65b31a6b-d930-5405-a282-e7625b84b8b7','73aca64d-c4ca-52b7-8720-1c1105faaed7',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an attempt to take the ball from an opponent in a game such as football','[ countable ]',null,'تلاش برای گرفتن توپ از حریف در یک بازی مانند فوتبال','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('df6e75fa-6622-552a-a554-f18bb4d6febb','73aca64d-c4ca-52b7-8720-1c1105faaed7',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a player in American football who stops other players by tackling them or preventing them from moving forward','[ countable ]',null,'بازیکنی در فوتبال آمریکایی که با تکل زدن به بازیکنان دیگر یا جلوگیری از حرکت رو به جلو آنها را متوقف می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('a260f0d3-3bc8-5835-8858-aa8941c55eb1','73aca64d-c4ca-52b7-8720-1c1105faaed7',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the equipment used in some sports and activities , especially fishing','[ uncountable ]',null,'تجهیزات مورد استفاده در برخی ورزش ها و فعالیت ها به ویژه ماهیگیری','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('8f096123-5377-523a-83db-eb582a05cfe2','73aca64d-c4ca-52b7-8720-1c1105faaed7',4,null,null,'spoken & written','ropes and pulley s (= wheels ) used for lifting heavy things','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'طناب و قرقره (= چرخ) که برای بلند کردن اجسام سنگین استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('0ae52485-3cd4-5de9-889a-6fbf4e569ab3','73aca64d-c4ca-52b7-8720-1c1105faaed7',5,null,null,'informal','a man’s sexual organs','[ uncountable ]',null,'اندام های جنسی مرد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('292e9379-574d-54ea-b35d-8e26dd2d8e76','8c248bc7-fff9-59bc-bffe-c237a69d2af6',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a natural ability to do something well','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'استعداد، نبوغ؛ استعداد (موسیقی)؛ استعداد (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have talent Greg has a real talent for drawing.','show talent Zach was the only one who showed any natural talent.','use your talents They have been using their artistic talents to brighten up the school.','develop your talent Education allows people to develop their talents to the full.','waste your talents They felt their son was wasting his talents and his time.','somebody’s talents flourish (= develop successfully ) The school created an atmosphere in which young talent could flourish.','great/considerable/exceptional talent He had a great talent for making money.','real talent She has real talent and with a little help she could go far.','natural talent Ronaldo is a player of immense natural talent.','raw talent (= used to describe someone with natural ability who has not had much training ) He’s got lots of raw talent but he needs a good coach.','a hidden talent Have a go – you may discover a hidden talent!','musical/artistic/creative etc talent It was at school that Brian’s musical talents were spotted.','a talent contest/show/competition Don’t assume winning a talent contest is a passport to success.','a wealth of talent (= a large amount of talent ) There’s a wealth of musical talent in New York and other large American cities.','a pool of talent (= lots of talented people ) Employers can draw on an enormous pool of talent in this area.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He has a lot of talent , and his work is fresh and interesting.","translation":"او استعداد زیادی دارد و کارش تازه و جالب است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001846406.mp3"},{"sentence":"She showed a talent for acting at an early age.","translation":"او در سنین پایین استعداد بازیگری را نشان داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001846442.mp3"},{"sentence":"a persuasive speaker with a natural talent for leadership","translation":"یک سخنران متقاعد کننده با استعداد طبیعی برای رهبری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001846420.mp3"},{"sentence":"His latest book reveals hidden talents .","translation":"آخرین کتاب او استعدادهای نهفته را آشکار می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001846424.mp3"},{"sentence":"Sadly, she inherited none of her father’s musical talent .","translation":"متأسفانه، او هیچ یک از استعدادهای موسیقیایی پدرش را به ارث نبرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001846428.mp3"},{"sentence":"Your brother is a man of many talents .","translation":"برادر شما مردی با استعداد است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001846432.mp3"},{"sentence":"There’s a wealth of talent in English football.","translation":"استعدادهای زیادی در فوتبال انگلیس وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001846436.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('0d3ac3c2-4474-58dc-a1ef-7b8fefc06684','8c248bc7-fff9-59bc-bffe-c237a69d2af6',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a person or people with a natural ability or skill','[ uncountable ]',null,'شخص یا افرادی با توانایی یا مهارت طبیعی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have talent Greg has a real talent for drawing.','show talent Zach was the only one who showed any natural talent.','use your talents They have been using their artistic talents to brighten up the school.','develop your talent Education allows people to develop their talents to the full.','waste your talents They felt their son was wasting his talents and his time.','somebody’s talents flourish (= develop successfully ) The school created an atmosphere in which young talent could flourish.','great/considerable/exceptional talent He had a great talent for making money.','real talent She has real talent and with a little help she could go far.','natural talent Ronaldo is a player of immense natural talent.','raw talent (= used to describe someone with natural ability who has not had much training ) He’s got lots of raw talent but he needs a good coach.','a hidden talent Have a go – you may discover a hidden talent!','musical/artistic/creative etc talent It was at school that Brian’s musical talents were spotted.','a talent contest/show/competition Don’t assume winning a talent contest is a passport to success.','a wealth of talent (= a large amount of talent ) There’s a wealth of musical talent in New York and other large American cities.','a pool of talent (= lots of talented people ) Employers can draw on an enormous pool of talent in this area.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Britain’s footballing talent","translation":"استعداد فوتبال بریتانیا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000613907.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('24e16427-70c7-55e4-8474-03ae7989a324','8c248bc7-fff9-59bc-bffe-c237a69d2af6',3,null,null,'informal','sexually attractive people','[ uncountable ]',null,'افراد جذاب جنسی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have talent Greg has a real talent for drawing.','show talent Zach was the only one who showed any natural talent.','use your talents They have been using their artistic talents to brighten up the school.','develop your talent Education allows people to develop their talents to the full.','waste your talents They felt their son was wasting his talents and his time.','somebody’s talents flourish (= develop successfully ) The school created an atmosphere in which young talent could flourish.','great/considerable/exceptional talent He had a great talent for making money.','real talent She has real talent and with a little help she could go far.','natural talent Ronaldo is a player of immense natural talent.','raw talent (= used to describe someone with natural ability who has not had much training ) He’s got lots of raw talent but he needs a good coach.','a hidden talent Have a go – you may discover a hidden talent!','musical/artistic/creative etc talent It was at school that Brian’s musical talents were spotted.','a talent contest/show/competition Don’t assume winning a talent contest is a passport to success.','a wealth of talent (= a large amount of talent ) There’s a wealth of musical talent in New York and other large American cities.','a pool of talent (= lots of talented people ) Employers can draw on an enormous pool of talent in this area.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('9778b112-14d0-50f2-ade4-fd2a20e05746','ffbe35d7-a2fd-5bf2-9d58-87219b3a3807',1,'aim','هدف','spoken & written','something that you are trying to achieve , such as a total , an amount , or a time',null,null,'هدف، مقصود؛ هدف (پرتاب)؛ هدف (بازار)',array['goal']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['meet a target (= achieve what you want to achieve ) The government wants to meet its target of building three million new homes by 2020.','reach/achieve/hit a target (= meet it ) They achieved their target with just days to spare.','set a target The company has set ambitious business targets.','exceed a target (= achieve more than you wanted to ) We have exceeded our target of £200,000.','fall short of a target (= achieve less than you wanted to ) Car production at the plant has fallen short of its target by 5%.','ambitious/high The targets they have set themselves are hugely ambitious.','modest (= not very high ) The Kyoto Protocol set fairly modest targets for reductions in greenhouse gases.','achievable/realistic The target is achievable, but only by hard work.','a financial target Both businesses exceeded their financial targets.','a sales target I’m confident we will meet our sales target by the end of the year.','a growth target The company’s growth targets have been achieved for the last three years.','a target date There is no target date set for completion of the new project.','a target figure The government has set a target figure of 6.2%']::text[],'[{"sentence":"demanding financial targets","translation":"خواستار اهداف مالی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616041.mp3"},{"sentence":"the target of a one-third reduction in road accidents","translation":"هدف کاهش یک سوم تصادفات جاده ای است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616046.mp3"},{"sentence":"Higher degrees in English are a target for foreign students.","translation":"مقاطع بالاتر در زبان انگلیسی هدف دانشجویان خارجی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001827634.mp3"},{"sentence":"There is no target date for completion of the new project.","translation":"هیچ تاریخ هدفی برای تکمیل پروژه جدید وجود ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616047.mp3"},{"sentence":"The government may fail to meet (= achieve ) its target of recycling 25% of domestic waste.","translation":"دولت ممکن است نتواند به هدف خود یعنی بازیافت 25 درصد زباله های خانگی دست یابد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616051.mp3"},{"sentence":"Jiang set annual growth targets of 8–9%.","translation":"جیانگ اهداف رشد سالانه 8 تا 9 درصد را تعیین کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616058.mp3"},{"sentence":"The company says that growth of 10% is on target.","translation":"این شرکت می گوید که رشد 10 درصدی در نظر گرفته شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000582072.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('5765b520-42c2-56a2-a9b7-6f0cb8adaf22','ffbe35d7-a2fd-5bf2-9d58-87219b3a3807',2,'object of attack','هدف حمله','spoken & written','an object , person, or place that is deliberately chosen to be attacked',null,null,'یک شی، شخص یا مکانی که عمداً برای حمله انتخاب شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Railway stations are prime targets (= very likely targets ) for bombs.","translation":"ایستگاه‌های راه‌آهن اهداف اصلی (= اهداف بسیار محتمل) برای بمب‌ها هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616066.mp3"},{"sentence":"Cars without security devices are an easy target for the thief.","translation":"خودروهای بدون وسایل امنیتی یک هدف آسان برای سارق هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000582052.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('2dd5cebc-a4e2-540d-a35e-f1fabf41c3bf','ffbe35d7-a2fd-5bf2-9d58-87219b3a3807',3,'object of an action','موضوع یک عمل','spoken & written','the person or place that is most directly affected by an action , especially a bad one',null,null,'شخص یا مکانی که مستقیماً تحت تأثیر یک عمل، به ویژه یک عمل بد قرار می گیرد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The area has become a prime target for supermarket development.","translation":"این منطقه به یک هدف اصلی برای توسعه سوپرمارکت تبدیل شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616077.mp3"},{"sentence":"The country is a target of criticism for its human rights record.","translation":"این کشور به دلیل سابقه حقوق بشری خود هدف انتقاد قرار گرفته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616081.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('10f7fa6c-faa4-55b0-9e2c-88ab9960ce0e','ffbe35d7-a2fd-5bf2-9d58-87219b3a3807',4,'shooting','تیراندازی','spoken & written','something that you practise shooting at, especially a round board with circles on it',null,null,'چیزی که تمرین تیراندازی روی آن می کنید، مخصوصاً یک تخته گرد با دایره هایی روی آن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The area is used by the army for target practice .","translation":"این منطقه توسط ارتش برای تمرین هدف استفاده می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616085.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c217333b-ea91-53e9-9f36-641b9fccc058','ffbe35d7-a2fd-5bf2-9d58-87219b3a3807',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'target audience/group/area etc','هدف، مقصود؛ هدف (پرتاب)؛ هدف (بازار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
