('3ab0dfa5-ffd2-5918-abf2-f8c76d093151','1755a247-8248-5f32-9c48-a1a5e3b7156a',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make something have an effect on a particular limited group or area',null,null,'کاری کردن که چیزی روی یک گروه یا منطقه محدود خاص تأثیر بگذارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The advertisement was designed to target a mass audience.","translation":"این تبلیغات برای هدف قرار دادن مخاطبان انبوه طراحی شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616097.mp3"},{"sentence":"a new benefit targeted on low-income families","translation":"یک مزیت جدید برای خانواده های کم درآمد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000582109.mp3"},{"sentence":"The programme is targeted at improving the health of women of all ages.","translation":"هدف این برنامه بهبود سلامت زنان در تمام سنین است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616098.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('df043757-95e5-56b5-82d7-05384c169117','1755a247-8248-5f32-9c48-a1a5e3b7156a',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to aim something at a target',null,null,'هدف گرفتن چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The missiles are targeted at several key military sites.","translation":"این موشک ها چندین سایت مهم نظامی را هدف قرار می دهند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000582103.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('8f364a38-01cd-5df6-8867-1e13f59bb3a2','1755a247-8248-5f32-9c48-a1a5e3b7156a',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to choose a particular person or place to do something to, especially to attack them or criticize them',null,null,'انتخاب یک فرد یا مکان خاص برای انجام کاری، به ویژه برای حمله به آنها یا انتقاد از آنها','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"It’s clear that smaller, more vulnerable banks have been targeted.","translation":"واضح است که بانک های کوچکتر و آسیب پذیرتر هدف قرار گرفته اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000582113.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was targeted by terrorists for a second time last night.","translation":"وی شب گذشته برای دومین بار مورد هدف تروریست ها قرار گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616101.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('2779d7ee-fe4c-5c2e-8889-dc88a7d049c0','cfe64688-824e-5a16-87a1-f08da980d857',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a game for two people or two pairs of people who use racket s to hit a small soft ball backwards and forwards over a net',null,null,'تنیس، تنیس (ورزش)؛ تنیس (مسابقه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('948bb0b3-3b46-5a19-9ade-0e745423682c','11aa542a-6784-59c5-a91a-a73dbf4f651c',1,'fear','ترس','spoken & written','a feeling of extreme fear','[ uncountable ]',null,'وحشت، ترس شدید؛ دهشت (سیاسی)؛ وحشت (حالت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['sheer/pure terror (= complete and total terror ) The horse galloped off in sheer terror down the path.','absolute/stark terror (= extreme terror ) On his face was an expression of absolute terror.','mortal terror literary (= very great terror ) The crew was in mortal terror of drowning.','strike terror into somebody’s heart His fearsome appearance strikes terror into the hearts of his enemies.','flee in terror The children fled in terror as the barn caught fire.','scream/shriek in terror She jumped to her feet, screaming in terror.','live in terror Everyone lived in terror of the religious police.','inspire terror The main aim of suicide bombers is to inspire terror in the population.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"People fled in terror as fire tore through the building.","translation":"مردم با وحشت از ساختمان فرار کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626230.mp3"},{"sentence":"Shots rang out, and I screamed in terror .","translation":"صدای تیراندازی بلند شد و من از وحشت فریاد زدم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626234.mp3"},{"sentence":"We lived in terror of our father when he was drinking.","translation":"وقتی پدرمان مشروب می‌نوشید، ما در وحشت زندگی می‌کردیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626238.mp3"},{"sentence":"There was a look of sheer terror (= complete terror ) on his face.","translation":"وحشت محض (= وحشت کامل) در چهره اش بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626244.mp3"},{"sentence":"The sound of enemy planes struck terror into our hearts.","translation":"صدای هواپیماهای دشمن رعب و وحشت را در دل ما فرو برد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626251.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('3d075fb4-0a27-5615-980a-6fab85df8177','11aa542a-6784-59c5-a91a-a73dbf4f651c',2,'frightening situation','وضعیت ترسناک','spoken & written','an event or situation that makes people feel extremely frightened , especially because they think they may die','[ countable ]',null,'رویداد یا موقعیتی که باعث می شود مردم احساس ترس شدید کنند، به ویژه به این دلیل که فکر می کنند ممکن است بمیرند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['sheer/pure terror (= complete and total terror ) The horse galloped off in sheer terror down the path.','absolute/stark terror (= extreme terror ) On his face was an expression of absolute terror.','mortal terror literary (= very great terror ) The crew was in mortal terror of drowning.','strike terror into somebody’s heart His fearsome appearance strikes terror into the hearts of his enemies.','flee in terror The children fled in terror as the barn caught fire.','scream/shriek in terror She jumped to her feet, screaming in terror.','live in terror Everyone lived in terror of the religious police.','inspire terror The main aim of suicide bombers is to inspire terror in the population.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the terrors of war","translation":"وحشت های جنگ","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626254.mp3"},{"sentence":"Death holds no terrors for (= does not frighten ) me.","translation":"مرگ هیچ ترسی برای من (= نمی ترساند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626255.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('aaa90bae-1fa9-547c-8b4d-94b9fae0b4e9','11aa542a-6784-59c5-a91a-a73dbf4f651c',3,'violent action','اقدام خشونت آمیز','spoken & written','violent action for political purposes','[ uncountable ]',null,'اقدام خشونت آمیز برای اهداف سیاسی',array['terrorism']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['sheer/pure terror (= complete and total terror ) The horse galloped off in sheer terror down the path.','absolute/stark terror (= extreme terror ) On his face was an expression of absolute terror.','mortal terror literary (= very great terror ) The crew was in mortal terror of drowning.','strike terror into somebody’s heart His fearsome appearance strikes terror into the hearts of his enemies.','flee in terror The children fled in terror as the barn caught fire.','scream/shriek in terror She jumped to her feet, screaming in terror.','live in terror Everyone lived in terror of the religious police.','inspire terror The main aim of suicide bombers is to inspire terror in the population.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The resistance movement started a campaign of terror .","translation":"جنبش مقاومت کارزار ترور را آغاز کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000591813.mp3"},{"sentence":"The Red Army Faction tried to undermine the state by terror tactics .","translation":"فراکسیون ارتش سرخ سعی کرد با تاکتیک های تروریستی دولت را تضعیف کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626263.mp3"},{"sentence":"Pol Pot’s reign of terror in Cambodia","translation":"حکومت وحشت پل پوت در کامبوج","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001827731.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('91d1c5c2-4e93-5202-93ae-c5236118cf01','11aa542a-6784-59c5-a91a-a73dbf4f651c',4,'person','شخص','informal','a child who is difficult to control','[ countable ]',null,'کودکی که کنترل آن دشوار است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['sheer/pure terror (= complete and total terror ) The horse galloped off in sheer terror down the path.','absolute/stark terror (= extreme terror ) On his face was an expression of absolute terror.','mortal terror literary (= very great terror ) The crew was in mortal terror of drowning.','strike terror into somebody’s heart His fearsome appearance strikes terror into the hearts of his enemies.','flee in terror The children fled in terror as the barn caught fire.','scream/shriek in terror She jumped to her feet, screaming in terror.','live in terror Everyone lived in terror of the religious police.','inspire terror The main aim of suicide bombers is to inspire terror in the population.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"That Johnson kid’s a real little terror!","translation":"آن بچه جانسون یک وحشت کوچک واقعی است!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000591826.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('77a68ab9-9a7f-5f5b-ad85-ded648539bca','4fca9cc6-b1ad-5b26-a3d4-bd9ff5296782',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used to tell someone that you are grateful for something they have given you or done for you',null,null,'تشکر، ممنون؛ سپاس (خبر)؛ تشکر (سپاس)',array['thank you']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘Pass the salt, please ... thanks.’","translation":"\"نمک را بفرستید، لطفا... متشکرم.\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000593080.mp3"},{"sentence":"Thanks a lot for the drink.","translation":"خیلی ممنون بابت نوشیدنی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001629003.mp3"},{"sentence":"Thanks very much for your help.","translation":"از کمک شما بسیار سپاسگزارم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001629006.mp3"},{"sentence":"Many thanks for the lovely flowers.","translation":"خیلی ممنون بابت گلهای دوست داشتنی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001827764.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’d love to go to the party. Thanks for asking me.","translation":"من دوست دارم به مهمانی بروم. ممنون که از من پرسیدی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000593083.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('57b379e6-4cd5-53d3-9d6c-950ca19d8bad','4fca9cc6-b1ad-5b26-a3d4-bd9ff5296782',2,null,null,'spoken & written','used as a polite way of accepting something that someone has offered you',null,null,'به عنوان روشی مودبانه برای پذیرش چیزی که کسی به شما پیشنهاد کرده است استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘Do you want another cup of coffee?’ ‘Oh, thanks.’","translation":"«آیا یک فنجان قهوه دیگر می‌خواهی؟» «اوه، متشکرم.»","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000593096.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('0a4c9dba-f187-54d3-a903-df3db868330f','4fca9cc6-b1ad-5b26-a3d4-bd9ff5296782',3,null,null,'spoken','used when politely answering someone’s question',null,null,'هنگام پاسخ مودبانه به سؤال کسی استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘Hi, Bill, how are you?’ ‘Fine, thanks.’","translation":"«سلام، بیل، چطوری؟» «خوب، ممنون.»","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001629014.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('3ec9f4f5-dab9-5be0-8c1e-0104dcee4a8c','4fca9cc6-b1ad-5b26-a3d4-bd9ff5296782',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'no thanks',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('001cd4e0-9047-53d2-9d2a-1f45841dfac8','4fca9cc6-b1ad-5b26-a3d4-bd9ff5296782',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'thanks a lot',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('080f0616-22b7-555f-b8c8-2bd9c21ec198','4a6cac2c-d2b9-5517-977b-7893098fa131',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the things you say or do to show that you are grateful to someone',null,null,'تشکر، سپاسگزاری؛ تشکر (فرد)؛ سپاس (سپاس)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['express your thanks (= say that you are grateful ) I would like to express my thanks to you for all your support.','offer/extend your thanks to somebody (= thank someone publicly ) We would also like to extend our heartfelt thanks to the medical staff at Broadgreen Hospital.','give thanks (= thank God ) Let us give thanks for the beauty of the world.','thanks go to somebody Above all, our thanks go to Barbara Lambourne.','grateful thanks Our grateful thanks go to everyone who took part in the event.','sincere/heartfelt thanks Please accept my most sincere thanks for all your help.','special thanks Special thanks are due to John Bryden for his advice.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Joe got up and left without a word of thanks .","translation":"جو بلند شد و بدون تشکر از او رفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000593117.mp3"},{"sentence":"My thanks to all of you for your help.","translation":"من از همه شما برای کمک شما تشکر می کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001629032.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('d31ed013-9411-5290-bfc0-e3ba54c120a5','4a6cac2c-d2b9-5517-977b-7893098fa131',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'thanks to somebody/something','تشکر، سپاسگزاری؛ تشکر (فرد)؛ سپاس (سپاس)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['express your thanks (= say that you are grateful ) I would like to express my thanks to you for all your support.','offer/extend your thanks to somebody (= thank someone publicly ) We would also like to extend our heartfelt thanks to the medical staff at Broadgreen Hospital.','give thanks (= thank God ) Let us give thanks for the beauty of the world.','thanks go to somebody Above all, our thanks go to Barbara Lambourne.','grateful thanks Our grateful thanks go to everyone who took part in the event.','sincere/heartfelt thanks Please accept my most sincere thanks for all your help.','special thanks Special thanks are due to John Bryden for his advice.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e7b16886-a553-59c2-a612-9968ba92155e','4a6cac2c-d2b9-5517-977b-7893098fa131',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'no thanks to somebody/something','تشکر، سپاسگزاری؛ تشکر (فرد)؛ سپاس (سپاس)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['express your thanks (= say that you are grateful ) I would like to express my thanks to you for all your support.','offer/extend your thanks to somebody (= thank someone publicly ) We would also like to extend our heartfelt thanks to the medical staff at Broadgreen Hospital.','give thanks (= thank God ) Let us give thanks for the beauty of the world.','thanks go to somebody Above all, our thanks go to Barbara Lambourne.','grateful thanks Our grateful thanks go to everyone who took part in the event.','sincere/heartfelt thanks Please accept my most sincere thanks for all your help.','special thanks Special thanks are due to John Bryden for his advice.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('19d0ba9b-54ab-56f1-81fc-721ee9d54c15','760bec5b-9024-5c74-81a0-4b3dad4430ff',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used to refer to something that belongs to or is connected with people that have already been mentioned',null,null,'مال آن‌ها — ضمیر ملکی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"When our washing machine broke, our neighbours let us use theirs.","translation":"وقتی ماشین لباسشویی ما خراب شد، همسایه ها به ما اجازه دادند از ماشین لباسشویی ما استفاده کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000594137.mp3"},{"sentence":"Our house is number 25, and theirs is just opposite.","translation":"خانه ما شماره 25 است و خانه آنها درست روبروی آن.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001821622.mp3"},{"sentence":"We compared scores and found that theirs were higher than ours.","translation":"ما نمرات را مقایسه کردیم و متوجه شدیم که امتیاز آنها از ما بالاتر است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001821623.mp3"},{"sentence":"They shared the prize money with a friend of theirs .","translation":"آنها پول جایزه را با یکی از دوستانشان تقسیم کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001821626.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('562fc42b-277d-55ac-98e7-796ebfd89330','760bec5b-9024-5c74-81a0-4b3dad4430ff',2,null,null,'spoken & written','used when talking about someone who may be male or female , to avoid saying ‘his or hers’',null,null,'هنگام صحبت در مورد کسی که ممکن است مرد یا زن باشد، برای اجتناب از گفتن "مال او" استفاده می شود.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Everyone wants what is theirs by right.","translation":"هرکس به حق چیزی را که مال خودش است می خواهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001821633.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('12995862-802a-57f8-bb6f-a04b18bf1093','31ad917c-486f-5260-a79d-23b7d0167733',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an idea or set of ideas that is intended to explain something about life or the world , especially an idea that has not yet been proved to be true','[ countable ]',null,'نظریه، تئوری؛ نظریه (علمی)؛ نظریه (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['come up with/develop a theory These birds helped Darwin develop his theory of natural selection.','test a theory Researchers gave workers a questionnaire to test that theory.','prove a theory No evidence emerged to prove either theory.','support a theory Modern research strongly supports this theory.','disprove a theory ( also refute a theory formal ) (= show that it is wrong ) Later experiments seemed to disprove the theory.','discredit a theory (= make people stop believing in it ) These latest findings discredit his entire theory.','a scientific theory Scientific theories can be tested experimentally.','an economic theory His economic theory assumes that both labour and capital are perfectly mobile.','a conspiracy theory (= a theory that an event was the result of secret plan made by two or more people ) A variety of conspiracy theories question the official account of President Kennedy’s assassination.','a pet theory (= a personal theory that you strongly believe ) Each of them had his pet theory on what had caused the uprising.','the theory of evolution/relativity etc According to the theory of relativity, nothing can travel faster than light.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"different theories about how the brain works","translation":"نظریه های مختلف در مورد نحوه عملکرد مغز","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001629148.mp3"},{"sentence":"Darwin’s theory of evolution","translation":"نظریه تکامل داروین","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000594657.mp3"},{"sentence":"the theory that light is made up of waves","translation":"این نظریه که نور از امواج تشکیل شده است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000594660.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('d20ffc90-3a7d-5840-aa05-c073b7feda70','31ad917c-486f-5260-a79d-23b7d0167733',2,null,null,'spoken & written','general principles and ideas about a subject','[ uncountable ]',null,'اصول و ایده های کلی در مورد یک موضوع','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['come up with/develop a theory These birds helped Darwin develop his theory of natural selection.','test a theory Researchers gave workers a questionnaire to test that theory.','prove a theory No evidence emerged to prove either theory.','support a theory Modern research strongly supports this theory.','disprove a theory ( also refute a theory formal ) (= show that it is wrong ) Later experiments seemed to disprove the theory.','discredit a theory (= make people stop believing in it ) These latest findings discredit his entire theory.','a scientific theory Scientific theories can be tested experimentally.','an economic theory His economic theory assumes that both labour and capital are perfectly mobile.','a conspiracy theory (= a theory that an event was the result of secret plan made by two or more people ) A variety of conspiracy theories question the official account of President Kennedy’s assassination.','a pet theory (= a personal theory that you strongly believe ) Each of them had his pet theory on what had caused the uprising.','the theory of evolution/relativity etc According to the theory of relativity, nothing can travel faster than light.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Freudian theory has had a great influence on psychology.","translation":"نظریه فروید تأثیر زیادی بر روانشناسی داشته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000594666.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’m taking a course on political theory.","translation":"من در حال گذراندن دوره تئوری سیاسی هستم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001629155.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
